(25807, '??????????? ??????? ???????? ?????? ????????~!\n[BUTTON]=[????][1]\n[MENU]'),
(25900, 'Love is in the Air 1'),
(25901, 'Vegan Goblin in Goblin Camp asks you to gather and deliver 10 Miner Mole\'s teeth, and 1 Miner Mole\'s tail hairs to prove his love.\n(Search Burning Rock. Miner Mole\'s teeth and Miner Mole\'s tail hairs can be obtaine by defeating Miner Moles)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(25902, 'Hey good to see you! It\'s been a long time!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(25903, 'Hey! How have you been? What are you up too?\n[NEXT]'),
(25904, 'Ah! Well don\'t you worry. I\'m not hungry at the moment.\n[NEXT]'),
(25905, 'Good. What\'s going on?\n[NEXT]'),
(25906, 'I found someone that I really like. I\'m even thinking that she could be the "one". I\'m trying to sweep her off her feet and I know the perfect thing that\'ll do the job! A necklace made out of {color,yellow,Miner Mole\'s tail hair} and {color,yellow,Miner Mole\'s tooth} is the hottest thing around female goblins. [NAME], be a pal and help this old goblin in love please?\n[BUTTON]=[Sure why not? I\'ll help you out!][1]\n[BUTTON]=[You\'re on your own buddy!][2]'),
(25907, 'That was trough. Here you go, a tail hair and a tooth.\n[NEXT]'),
(25908, 'I can\'t believe you got them! Thank you so much!\nI\'ll have good chance to win her over now!\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(25909, 'It shouldn\'t be too hard for you. Come on, I mean you\'re pretty strong!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26000, 'Love is in the Air 2'),
(26001, 'Vegan Goblin in Goblin Camp asks you to gather and deliver 10 Miner Mole\'s teeth, and 1 Miner Mole\'s tail hairs to prove his love again.\n(Search Burning Rock. Miner Mole\'s teeth and Miner Mole\'s tail hairs can be obtaine by defeating Miner Moles)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26002, 'Nooooo! [NAME]! [NAME]!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26003, 'What\'s wrong? Did you get hurt or something?\n[NEXT]'),
(26004, 'No it\'s not that. You know those Miner Mole teeth and tail hairs you got for me? Well, I was on the way to my love Malabutia to confess my love with them. And that no good chief\'s girlfriend commended her thugs to rob me of those precious items. I couldn\'t do anything about it!\n[NEXT] '),
(26005, 'You just gave up confessing to her?\n[NEXT]'),
(26006, 'I\'m so sorry but, could you get me more {color,yellow,10 Miner Mole teeth} and {color,yellow,1 more Miner Mole tail hairs}? [NAME], since you are so strong it should be like walking in the park right? Please?\n[BUTTON]=[Fine. But this is the last time.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[You\'ll just lose it again! Forget it!][2]'),
(26007, 'Here, if you lose this, you are really on your own. You got that?\n[NEXT]'),
(26008, 'Yay! You are the greatest! Thank you so so so much!\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26009, 'My love Malabutia... Oh my precious Malabutia...\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26100, 'Malabutia\'s Headdress'),
(26101, 'You have acquired Malabutia\'s headress. Please give it to Vegan Goblin in Goblin Camp.\n(Search Goblin Camp)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26102, 'Hey Mr. Goblin! \n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26103, 'Hey [NAME]! What brings you here? Did you find some tasty mushrooms or something?\n[NEXT]'),
(26104, 'Huh? Well no... Anyways, did you confess your love to her?\n[NEXT]'),
(26105, 'I did but it didn\'t go too well. She said, we should just be friends. But you know what? We are greeting and acknowledging each other! For now just being able to talk to her and see her smiling yellow teeth is enough for me. I am happy in my own way.\n[NEXT]'),
(26106, 'Well... Really? I see...\nI guess you won\'t be needing this then huh?\n[NEXT]'),
(26107, 'What? Isn\'t that {color,yellow,Malabutia headdress} she lost? Where did you get it? Tell me!\n[NEXT]'),
(26108, 'Monster ate it? I would kill that foul beast! \nOh you saw the name engraved here huh? Wow, you know what? With this I am one step close to winning her over! Thank you so much! Hey this isn\'t much but have some of my mushrooms! Thank you!\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26109, 'What\'s up?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26200, 'Suspicious Spell of Destruction 1'),
(26201, 'Guard Nus of Elderine asks you to collect 5 Core Guardian\'s Teeth, 3 Core Guardian\'s Claws, 1 Core Guardian\'s Spine, and 30 Violets to produce a \'Spell of Destruction\'.\n(Search Burning Rock. You can obtain Core Guardian\'s Teeth, Core Guardian\'s Claws, Core Guardian\'s Spine, and Violets by defeating Core Guardians)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26202, 'Hehehehehe!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26203, 'What\'s with the weird laugh?\n[NEXT]'),
(26204, 'Eureka! I finally found out!\n[NEXT]'),
(26205, 'Found what out?\n[NEXT]'),
(26206, 'A powerful genocide spell! \nTake a good look at this scroll.\nWith {color,yellow,5 Core Guardian Teeth}, {color,yellow,3 Core Guardian Claws},{color,yellow,1 Core Guardian Spine}, and {color,yellow,30 Violets}, we can wipe every single Core Guardian out of Isya!\n[BUTTON]=[Really? It could be true. I\'ll give him a benefit of doubt][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Just stop, okay?][2]'),
(26207, 'Oh... My... God... here Nus... Why do I do this to myself?\n[NEXT]'),
(26208, 'Ah! Good job kid! You know your hard work will soon pay off! I\'m off to make that Spell of Destruction so see you later alright?\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26209, 'What\'s taking so long man? Skills! You need some skills kid!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26300, 'Suspicious Spell of Destruction 2'),
(26301, 'Guard Nus Elderine asks  you to collect 5 Ruby Guardian Front Teeth, 3 Ruby Guardian Claws, 1 Ruby Guardian Pelvis, and 50 Geraniums to produce a \'Spell of Destruction\'.\n(Search Burning Rock. Ruby Guardian Front Teeth, Ruby Guardian Claws, Ruby Guardian Pelvis, and Geraniums can be found by defeating Ruby Guardians) \n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26302, 'AH HAHAHAHA! WA HAHAHAHA!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26303, 'Hey, what\'s so funny? Did you finish making \'Spell of Destruction?\n[NEXT]'),
(26304, 'Huh? Oh you! When did you get here?\nAh hahaha, well... I kind of screwed up on the interpretation. It turns out that it\'s Ruby Guardian not Core Guardian and it\'s also their front teeth, claws, and pelvis... not what you got for me. Oh! Oh! you also need Geraniums, about 50 of them! You\'ll help our right? I mean you promised. \n[NEXT]'),
(26305, 'Wait a minute. That\'s kind of fishy.\nTell me the truth Nus! Is your spell legit?\n[NEXT]'),
(26306, 'Of course it is!!!\nYou don\'t think I\'m some kind of slimeball that uses good person like [NAME] to do my bidding do you?\nCome on please? \nI need {color,yellow,5 Ruby Guardian front Teeth,}\n{color,yellow,3 Ruby Guardian Claws,}\n{color,yellow,1 Ruby Guardain Pelvis} and last but not least {color,yellow,50 Geraniums}. \nI know you\'ll help. Please... Pretty Please?\n[BUTTON]=[Fine. stop saying \'pretty please\' you certainly aren\'t one!][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I\'m going to throw up. forget it Nus][2]'),
(26307, 'I feel like I\'ve been had.\nHere Nus.\n[NEXT]'),
(26308, 'Yes! You are the best!!!\nThank you so much [NAME]!!!\nYou know how I feel about you right? Okay you may go now. I need complete concentration and no distractions while making this spell.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26309, 'What\'s keeping you? Come on do it already gosh!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26400, 'Suspicious Spell of Destruction 3'),
(26401, 'Guard Nus of Elderine asks you to bring the Life Water from Guard Captain Shutian of Elderine.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26402, '[NAME]!!! [NAME]!!!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26403, 'What is it this time?\n[NEXT]'),
(26404, 'There is this really important ingredient that I need to complete a Spell of Destruction.\nCould you get it for me? I almost forgot about it you know.\nWithout it I don\'t think I can complete the spell. Life Water is what I need. I know {color,yellow,Captain Shutian} have one in his possesion. I just know captain won\'t just hand it out to me. But I know for a fact that captain trust you [NAME]. If you tell captain that you need the {color,yellow,Life Water} to revive a dying tree at an outskirt of the town, he\'ll gladly give it to you.\nYou can handle that right?\n[BUTTON]=[Got it dying tree. I\'ll be back][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Nope. I just can\'t do things like that Nus.][2]'),
(26405, 'Hello Captain Shutian.\nHow have you been?\n[NEXT]'),
(26406, 'Look who\'s here! Wow [NAME], what brings you here?\nHow\'s the saving the world business going for you? Everything well I presume?\n[NEXT]'),
(26407, 'Well, Yes considering...\nI do have a request to ask of you.\nI need a Life Water to save... Ah! That big tree outskirt of the town!\nIt just seems so weak these days.\n[NEXT]'),
(26408, 'I see... Well, sharing Life Water with you isn\'t a problem. You seem bit tense for some reason.\nHmm...\nYou know what I think? I think there isn\'t a tree to save. I think someone might have put you up to get a Life Water. You know what else? I believe this might be something to do with that recently lost pages of \'Forbidden Spells\'. Could you tell me the truth?\n[NEXT]'),
(26409, 'Well... it\'s...\nOh man... So it\'s because...\n[NEXT]'),
(26410, 'Don\'t worry, tell me. I promise I won\'t be too harsh on whomever it is.\n[NEXT]'),
(26411, 'Okay... I\'m sorry. Truth is that Nus put me up to this.\nHe said he needed a Core Guardian\'s spines, teeth. Something about eyes and Life Water.\n[NEXT]'),
(26412, 'I am bit disappointed at you for lying for him. But you had to do what you had to do for your friend, and I respect that.\nBut that Nus need to be taught a lesson for making you lie in behalf of him. \nI think I know what\'s he up to. It seems he\'s in a process of creating a \'Pet Monster\'. It only lives for one day and, are very obedient to its creator. However creating a disposable pet for one day of joy is very cruel thing to do. It seems Nus is in need to be taught a very serious lesson. \nWhy don\'t you take this back to him. Tell him that this is the \'Life Water\' that he seeks. I\'m sure it\'ll amuse you and will certaintly teach him a lesson.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26413, 'Did you get it?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26414, 'Suspicious Spell of Destruction 4'),
(26415, 'Guard Captain Shutian asks you to deliver the fake Life Water to Guard Nus in Elderine.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26416, 'Why don\'t you take this to Nus.\nTell him it\'s the Life Water that he seeks, I\'m sure the outcome will amuse you.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26417, 'Hey Nus!\nHere, I got you that {color,yellow,Life Water} you are looking for.\n[NEXT]'),
(26418, 'You\'re back finally!\nI\'ve been waiting for it. You sure took along time.\nWell, thanks.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26419, 'Are you telling me that you don\'t know where {color,yellow,Guard Nus} is?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26500, 'Suspicious Spell of Destruction 5'),
(26501, 'Elderine Guard Nus asks you to collect 50 Ruby Guardian Hairs, 20 Ruby Guardian Hides, 2 of Ruby Guardian Eyes. \n(Search Burning Rock. Ruby Guardian Hairs, Ruby Guardian Hides, Ruby Guardian Eyes can be obtained by defeating Ruby Guardians) \n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26502, 'What!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26503, 'Hey what\'s going on?\n[NEXT]'),
(26504, 'Oh no! I\'m so so sorry! I got the wrong ingredients.\nPlease this is the last time! Please!\nCome on be a pal!\n[NEXT]'),
(26505, 'You on something Nus? No way I\'ll help your sorry behind.\nForget it!\n[NEXT]'),
(26506, 'Please...\nI\'m really sorry... but this really is the last time. If not for me, do it for Elderine.\nPlease...\n[NEXT]'),
(26507, 'Are you crying? What is wrong with you really?\nFine this is the last time!\nIf you think you can use me again, I will destroy you!\n[NEXT]'),
(26508, 'Thank you! Thank you so much!\nI won\'t forget really!\nI need {color,yellow,50 Ruby Guardian\'s Hair}, {color,yellow,20 Ruby Guardian\'s Hides}, {color,yellow,2 of Ruby Guardian\'s Eyes}, I already have a {color,yellow,Life Water} you got me last time so I\'m good with that.\nWell, what are you waiting for? Get going!\n[BUTTON]=[Fine, let\'s do this.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Forget it, let\'s kill him now.][2]'),
(26509, 'Nus! I got your things.\n[NEXT]'),
(26510, 'Finally!\nMan, you sure took some time huh?\nOh I got what I needed. You may go now.\n[NEXT]'),
(26511, 'Say what?!\nI\'ve been slaving over this and you are not going to show me what you are going to make? Man that\'s low, even from you!\n[NEXT]'),
(26512, 'You want to see it?\nWell, I can\'t really show...\nFine! Step back and stand over there.\nPOW!!!\n(An unsavory blue smoke is emitting from Nus\' hand)\nIt can\'t be! It can\'t fail! what happened?\nWhat in the world!\n(Nus\'s face is turned into a Ruby Guardian\'s face)\n[NEXT]'),
(26513, 'Nus... your face...\nWhahahahahaha! Serves you right!\nYou were going to make a Pet Monster with all the things I got you huh? Trying to fool me! Well, I fool you! Captain Shutian saw through your scheme like fish in a fishbowl and got you a fake Life Water! Ha!\n[NEXT]'),
(26514, 'I\'ve been caught!\nSorry for that!\nBut you scammed me too [NAME]!\nWhat am I going to do? I can\'t go out looking like a monster!\n[NEXT]'),
(26515, 'You should\'ve thought about that before you try to scam me.\nRemember fool me once, shame on you, but fool me twice shame on me. You will eat through a straw for rest of your life if you try to pull a stunt like this agiain! Got it?\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26516, 'Why are you still here?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26600, 'A Mole Wine'),
(26601, 'Storage Keeper Curly of Uruga asks you to collect 60 Mine Mole\'s forelegs to produce a Mole Wine which is rumored to have a healing properties. \n(Search Burning Rock. Mine Mole\'s forelegs can be obtainied by defeating Mine Moles)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26602, 'Hey it\'s been a while!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26603, 'Hey Curly, what\'s going on? You are looking good over there, been working out?\n[NEXT]'),
(26604, 'Really? I do? Nice, it\'s actually working!\nWell, no work out, but I\'ve drank couple glasses of neighbor\'s Mole Wine, and I have so much energy and I feel great! Well, I kind of want to make my own Mole Wine and I need your help.\n[NEXT]'),
(26605, 'Help with what? Making Mole Wine?\n[NEXT]'),
(26606, 'Yes please?\nI\'ve heard forelegs of Miner Moles are the best suited for the wine. Can you collect {color,yellow,60 Miner Mole\'s forelegs}? I will make it worth your trouble. I promise.\n[BUTTON]=[Sure, not a problem.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Do you know how tough those moles are?][2]'),
(26607, 'Curly, here you go.\n[NEXT]'),
(26608, 'Wow, Great!\nWhen the wine ages and mature in few years, I\'ll share them with you too. So keep your fingers crossed.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26609, 'I said {color,yellow,forelegs} not hind legs! \n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26700, 'Burning Heart'),
(26701, 'Stone Merchant Thompson in Burning Rock asks you to collect 3 Flame Spirit\'s heart.\n(Search Burning Rock. You can obtain Flame Spirit\'s hearts by defeating Flame Spirits)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW-REWARD]'),
(26702, 'Hey wait, hang on.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26703, 'Oh... Hello how are you?\nI\'m [NAME], how do you do?\n[NEXT]'),
(26704, 'I\'m Thompson. Are you swinging by town by any chance?\nCould you take me with you?\n[NEXT]'),
(26705, 'Huh? What?\n[NEXT]'),
(26706, 'I\'m kidding, just joking haha... No sense of humor I see.\nI\'m just home-sick that\'s all...\nBy the way, have you ever heard a monster called Flamespirit?\n[NEXT]'),
(26707, 'Hmm... I think so.\n[NEXT]'),
(26708, 'What do you mean by you think so? Either you have or haven\'t, that\'s a real answer. Kids these days are so indecisive.\nWell, anyways could you get me a heart of a Flamespirit? I\'m not looking for an handout. I will pay for your trouble. \nI want to return home as soon as possible but that stingy Maxuter wouldn\'t let me go home until I meet my quota. So it got me thinking. I know for a fact that those {color,yellow,Flamespirit\'s heart} burns for days. Think about it... for days it burns. It\'s equivalent to couple days worth of firewood! \nSo could you please get me {color,yellow,3 Flamespirit\'s hearts}?\n[BUTTON]=[I don\'t like his attitude but since he\'s paying, why not?][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Get it yourself, o\' decisive one!][2]'),
(26709, 'Here you go. It\'s really hot.\n[NEXT]'),
(26710, 'Hot hot!\nBe gentle! What\'s wrong with you huh? You got no finesse at all! Talk about one barbaric brute! No wonder you are in your line of work! Take this and go away!\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26711, 'To go home, I need the dough!\nI have a contract to keep with Maxuter! Unlike you, I like to keep my promises! Who in the right mind will venture out to places like this? \n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26800, 'Crossing a path with Julian'),
(26801, 'Item Merchant Julian in Burning wishes to speak with you.\n(Search Burning Rock)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26802, 'Hello.\nI haven\'t seen you around here before!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26803, 'How do you do?\n[NEXT]'),
(26804, 'How do you do yourself? Haha... I\'m Julian.\nHey you must know what you are doing, since you are traveling this way. Don\'t be a stranger around here.\n[NEXT]'),
(26805, 'Sure...\nWell, anyways how did you ended up here? Like you said, this isn\'t a safest places around.\n[NEXT]'),
(26806, 'Hahaha, I know the lands around here very well. This place doesn\'t really scare me. I know many people are terrified of this place and avoid it like a bubanic plague but it\'s like my backyard.\n[NEXT]'),
(26807, 'I see...\n(I have an idea who he is referring to)\n[NEXT]'),
(26808, 'Well, if you have any question about this neck of woods, come to me. I\'m surprisingly well-informed.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26809, 'What?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26900, 'Blue Burning Heart'),
(26901, 'Item Merchant Julian in Burning Rock asks you to collect 1 Blue Burning Heart and bring it to Furniture Shop Owner Forest Tim in Uruga.\n(Search Burning Rock. Blue Burning Heart can be obtained by defeating Flame Spirits)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26902, 'Julian!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(26903, 'Hey you\'re back! What\'s up?\n[NEXT]'),
(26904, 'Well, I acquired something really odd.\nI remember that you said something about knowing a lot of things.\n[NEXT]'),
(26905, 'If you got it around here, sure I probably know about it. Let\'s have a look.\n[NEXT]'),
(26906, 'Here, I got this from Flamespirits.\n[NEXT]'),
(26907, 'Wow! It\'s a {color,yellow,blue heart}.\nFlamespirits are descendants of ancient spark souls. I just can\'t believe there are still Flamespirits out there with this kind of hearts. It\'s too bad that, they don\'t have a proper mind to go with the heart. It\'s best to hand it over the Soul Clan. Do you know of {color,yellow,Furniture Shop Owner Forest Tim} in {color,yellow,Uruga}? Give it to him and he\'ll take care of it. \n[BUTTON]=[Give this heart to Tim? Okay.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I\'m going to keep it.][2]'),
(26908, 'Hey! It\'s been a while.\n[NEXT]'),
(26909, 'Hey! [Name]! \nWhat brings you here? \nWhat do you have in your hands? That\'s the heart of an exalted spirit! \nAnd it\'s still burning! It means it\'s a rare spark soul. Where did you ever find this?!\nYou got it from a Flamespirit?\nI feel the pain of the spark soul.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(26910, 'Well, be on your way then.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27000, 'Maxuter'),
(27001, 'Merchant Master Maxuter in Burning Rock wishes to speak with you.\n(Search Burning Rock)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27002, 'Good to see you adventurer!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27003, 'Hi, I\'m [NAME], what\'s your name?\n[NEXT]'),
(27004, 'My name is Merchant Master Maxuter. I oversee all merchants around here. You possess a great skills, since you are standing here.\n[NEXT]'),
(27005, 'Well... not that great.\nI just followed where my feet take me.\n[NEXT]'),
(27006, 'I see that you also possess a humbleness as well.\nI certainly do hope our paths crosses again. \nIf you run into any trouble, let me know. I\'ll try to help out as much as my capacity allows to.\nI hope you extend same courtesy likewise.\n[NEXT]'),
(27007, 'Thank you.\n[NEXT]'),
(27008, 'May Teva walk with every step you take.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27009, 'What is it?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27100, 'A Kid from the Mines 1'),
(27101, 'Town Chief Adrian of Uruga asks you to collect 1 Marine\'s Memento.\n(Search Burning Rock. Marine\'s Memento can be obtained by defeating Kidmons)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27102, '[NAME]. Welcome.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27103, 'Hello chief. You were looking for me?\n[NEXT]'),
(27104, 'Yes [NAME], It seems that I am in need of your assistance.\nA disturbing letter from Burning Rock arrived today. It\'s from a good friend of mine , it seems that my friend witnessed a horrible event near the abandoned miner\'s town.\n[NEXT]'),
(27105, 'You are talking about that ghost town near the mines. What do you mean by a horrible events?\n[NEXT]'),
(27106, 'Well...\nA human turned to... \nHow do I put this? Well... turned to a monster.\n[NEXT]'),
(27107, 'Really? How\'s that possible?\n[NEXT]'),
(27108, 'Making it worse... that monster... that person who turned was a boy. A child who used to reside at the miner\'s town.\nWhew...\nIf this is even remotely possible, and if it really did happened... \nI really need to ask you a big favor [NAME]. If in fact, the boy is from the miner\'s town, I\'m sure there is something to link him to that town and prove his origin. \nPlease help me.\n[BUTTON]=[Leave it to me.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[That\'s too horrible, I\'m sorry I just can\'t.][2]'),
(27109, 'Chief Adrian, I found this at the site.\n(Handing over an old locket type necklace with faded photo of elegant lady)\n[NEXT]'),
(27110, 'Hmm... It\'s someone\'s memento.\nThere is an inscription. Looks like a name... "Marine".\nShe must be from that miner\'s town.\nI guess we do need to search for more concrete clues.\nThank you.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27111, 'It seems an unfortunate events are plaguing my days.\nI haven\'t smiled in a long time.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27200, 'A Kid from the Mines 2'),
(27201, 'Town Chief Adrian of Uruga asks you to collect 20 Kidmon\'s Hairs, and 1 Torn Piece of Garment.\n(Search Burning Rock. Kidmon\'s Hairs and Torn Piece of Garment can be obtained by defeating Kidmons.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27202, '[NAME]. \n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27203, 'Did you summon me?\n[NEXT]'),
(27204, 'Thank you for coming in such a short notice.\nI\'ve been investigating further into the monster at mine issue.\nI was able to find out the type of monster in question. It seems this Kidmon resembles awful like a child named Ray, who used to reside at the miner\'s town. However, according to former miner\'s town folks, Ray was killed when the that town was flourishing. Basically, it means Ray didn\'t turned into a monster.\nI guess more investigation is needed.\nThat\'s why I have call you here.\n[NEXT]'),
(27205, 'I see... That\'s a good news.\nWell, how can I help out?\n[NEXT]'),
(27206, 'I need to analyze the properties of the monster.\nCould I trouble you for {color,yellow,20 Kidmon\'s Hair} and {color,yellow,1 Torn Piece of Kidmon\'s Garment}?\n[BUTTON]=[Of course.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Sorry. I\'m kind of busy.][2]'),
(27207, 'Chief! Here it is.\n[NEXT]'),
(27208, 'Let\'s see...\nYes, it\'ll do.\nThank you for your effort. It\'ll help greatly. I\'m going to go analyze these.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27209, 'No more of these awful events should happen anymore.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27300, 'A Kid from the Mines 3'),
(27301, 'Town Chief Adrian of Uruga asks you to deliver Adrian\'s letter, and 1 Torn Piece of Kidmon\'s Garment to Merchant Master Maxuter in Burning Rock.\n(Search Burning Rock)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27302, '[NAME]! You came!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27303, 'Hey chief! You look happy and cheerful!\nAnything good happened?\n[NEXT]'),
(27304, 'Yes, yes... I do have some good news.\nI\'m sure it\'ll be good news to you too [NAME], but it isn\'t 100% concrete.\nIf the story can be verified by Maxuter, it\'ll be legitimate news. \nCould you take this {color,yellow,letter} and the {color,yellow,Torn Piece of Kidmon\'s Garment} to {color,yellow,Merchant Master Maxuter} in {color,yellow,Burning Rock}? I\'m sure he\'ll be able to tell you the whole story.\n[BUTTON]=[Of course.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Are you crazy? Burning Rock? Forget it.][2]'),
(27305, 'Hello, Mr. Maxuter.\nI\'ve brought you a letter from Chief Adrian.\n[NEXT]'),
(27306, 'Ah! I\'ve been waiting.\nWell, let\'s have a look. This is good news.\nThis imposter cannot possibly be related to human. It seems this monster mimicked appearance of a child. I belive this monster derived from ancient monster called \'Monte-Monte\' which played a trick on human by mimicking our looks. It seems while in mimicked stage, the monster had a trouble and stuck looking like a child. Thank you for all your trouble. Without you, this mystery could not have solved.\nThank you.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27307, 'Please go visit {color,yellow,Merchant Master Maxuter} who resides in {color,yellow,Burning Rock}.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27400, 'Please help us recover our memories 1'),
(27401, 'Merchant Master Maxuter in Burning Rock ask you to collect 1 Old Teddy Bear, 1 Gleaming Orb, and 1 Broken Picture Frame. \n(Search Burning Rock. You can obtain Old Teddy Bear, Gleaming Orb, and Broken Picture Frame by defeating Kidmons, Miners, and Kart Miners. \n[LINE] \n[SHOW_REWARD] '),
(27402, 'How are you today? You look well as always.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27403, 'Yes I try to keep myself fit. Hehehe.\nYou seem busy, is there are a lot of things going on here?\n[NEXT]'),
(27404, 'Yes, we have many request coming this way so...\nAh! Could you possibly help us out then?\n[NEXT]'),
(27405, 'Huh? What types of work?\n[NEXT]'),
(27406, 'As you probably know, this Miner\'s Town used to be once flourishing town. However, surge of monster attacks and overflowing magmas driven all town\'s folks out in haste. They had to leave in hurry, so they left many precious belongings behind. Most of the request is to retrieve such items for formal town occupants.\n[NEXT]'),
(27407, 'I see... items filled with memories...\n[NEXT]'),
(27408, 'Yes... \nI\'m sure it can be found amongst {color,yellow,Kidmons}, {color,yellow,Miners}, and {color,yellow,Kart Miners}. They sure do like to collect any discarded items. \nWell, this is a retrieval request from Mons family from Roumen. \nYou must find an {color,yellow,Old Teddy Bear}, a {color,yellow,Gleaming Orb}, and a {color,yellow,Broken Picture Frame} for them. \nOf course you will be awarded for your trouble. \n[BUTTON]=[Sure, I\'ll definately help out!][1] \n[BUTTON]=[I have enough cash for now, no thanks.][2] '),
(27409, 'I\'ve found them all!\n[NEXT]'),
(27410, 'You certainly are fast! Amazing! You found all of them while with our full capacity, we were only able to find two articles.\nYou certaintly are good! I hope you\'ll help out again next time!\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27411, 'We too are busy at taking care of all these floods of requests.\nWe are even taking mercenary requests.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27500, 'Please help to recover our memories 2'),
(27501, 'Merchant Master Maxuter in Burning Rock asks you to collect 1 Gray Scarf, 1 Worn-out Glove, and 1 Broken Vase.\n(Search Burning Rock. Gray Scarf, Worn-out Glove, and Broken Vase. from Skeleton Miners, Miners and Kart Miners.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27502, 'I received another request.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27503, 'Is this something I can take on?\n[NEXT]'),
(27504, 'Yes, I believe so.\nIt\'s from the Kaira couple from Uruga.\nYou would need to retrieve {color,yellow,1 Gray Scar}, {color,yellow,1 Worn-out Glove}, and {color,yellow,1 Broken Vase} from {color,yellow,Miners}, {color,yellow,Skeleton Miners}, and {color,yellow,Kart Miners}.\n[BUTTON]=[Sure thing.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I don\'t want to waste my time.][2]'),
(27505, 'Maxuter, I got them.\n[NEXT]'),
(27506, 'You came back. What an amazing performance.\nI hope you can help out in future as well.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27507, 'You can\'t buy memories with money or power.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27600, 'Please help to recover our memories 3'),
(27601, 'Merchant Master Maxuter in Burning Rock asks you to find his Old Music Box. \n(Search Burning Rock. You can obtain an Old Music Box by defeating Undead Miners.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27602, '[NAME]. Thank you for coming back.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27603, 'You are very welcome. So what\'s going on?\n[NEXT]'),
(27604, 'Well... I have a personal favor to ask of you...\n[NEXT]'),
(27605, 'A favor?\n[NEXT]'),
(27606, 'A long time ago, I was a member of this miner\'s village. It was so long ago, that I remember vaguely. But I do remember this very clearly. That fateful day when all had to flee this village, I lost my mother. I remember my mother\'s embrace, protecting me from the hot flames. I also remember my father\'s hand pulling me away from my mother\'s hardening body. \nWell... it is long ago and I only remember bits and pieces. But I do remember this very clearly. It\'s a sound of my mother\'s music box.\n[NEXT]'),
(27607, 'A music box?\n[NEXT]'),
(27608, 'Yes. \nI remember the melody emitting from that music box and the fading sound of my mother\'s laughter. \nIt\'s only a memory that I still retain about my mother. \nCould you please find that {color,yellow,Old Music Box}?\nI know that it won\'t be an easy task.\n[BUTTON]=[Of course! Leave it to me.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Not an easy task? Just get a new one.][2]'),
(27609, 'Maxuter! I\'ve found your music box!\n[NEXT]'),
(27610, '(Slowly opens the music box... mirror inside and the spinning doll have been broken long ago, but it still starts to play the melody. The melody emitting from the box may not be perfect and sounds out of tune, but while listening to it, Maxuter wipes his tears several times...)\nMother....\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27611, 'Its melody still haunts my ears. But I\'m afraid that I\'ll slowly forget the sounds.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue[1]\n[MENU]'),
(27700, 'Throw those Gems!'),
(27701, 'Stone Merchant Thompson in Burning Rock asks you to collect 30 Crystal Ores. \n(Search Burning Rock. Crystal Ores can be obtained by defeating Miners)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27702, 'You know the monsters called Miners right?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27703, 'Yes I do.\n[NEXT]'),
(27704, 'There is a rumor that those little monsters uses a very useful attacks!\n[NEXT]'),
(27705, 'What do you mean by useful attacks?\n[NEXT]'),
(27706, 'It chugs gemstones at you!\nThose little things collect gemstones on their spare time and throw them at people who pass by. \nGemstones? Is it worth it?\nHey can you collect {color,yellow,30 Crystal Ores} from those {color,yellow,Miners}. I really got to get rich quick and leave this awful place.\n[BUTTON]=[Fine, but it\'ll cost you.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Get it yourself!][2]'),
(27707, 'Here. That was tough.\n[NEXT]'),
(27708, 'Ha! You really went to get them?\nHey! What\'s with the attitude?\nFine I\'ll pay up! Who said I wanted your charity anyways?\nHere take this and beat it!\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27709, 'What\'s keeping you? Man seriously kids these day are so lazy!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27800, 'Safety Helmet Required!'),
(27801, 'Blacksmith Hans of Uruga asks you to collect 40 Safety Helmets for his construction project. \n(Search Burning Rock. Safety Helmets can be obtained by defeating Undead Miners)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27802, 'Hey welcome.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27803, 'Hello, Mr. Hans. How have you been?\nI heard you have some good news.\n[NEXT]'),
(27804, 'Oh so you have heard?\nWell, I\'ve been elected as a safety inspector for all construction right here in Uruga. \n[NEXT]'),
(27805, 'Well, that means your efforts has been respected by others.\nIt\'s great!\n[NEXT]'),
(27806, 'Thank you for your kind words.\nWell, speaking of that matter, I\'ve been thinking of providing a safety helmet for all workers free of charge. \nOnly thing is that, I\'m bit short on Safety Helmets these days. I was wondering if you could get me {color,yellow,40 Safety Helmets}? \nIt\'ll help out a lot!\n[BUTTON]=[Sure. That\'s not a problem.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I just don\'t want to.][2]'),
(27807, 'Mr. Hans! I got those safety helmets for you.\n[NEXT]'),
(27808, 'Oh thank you.\n[NAME], you certainly is good. Thank you.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27809, 'Did you go to Miner\'s Town yet?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27900, 'Picks are optional'),
(27901, 'Blacksmith Hans of Uruga asks you to collect 20 Undead Miners Heavy Picks to begin construction.\n(Search Burning Rock. Undead Miners Heavy Picks can be obtained by defeating Undead Miners)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27902, 'Wow, you came.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(27903, 'What is it Hans? You were looking for me again?\n[NEXT]'),
(27904, 'I\'ve been looking for some equipment for the construction, and unfortunately I don\'t think I can meet the deadline at the current state.\nThis really isn\'t good, considering I am in charge of everything related to construction. \nSo I was wondering if you could find me {color,yellow,20 Undead Miners Heavy Picks}? \nI\'ll reward you handsomely, of course .\n[BUTTON]=[Sure thing.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Liar! You never pay enough! Forget it.][2]'),
(27905, 'Hey Mr. Hans here\'s your pick. Man it\'s heavy!\n[NEXT]'),
(27906, 'Thank you so much! This would help so much!\nI appreicate it so much.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(27907, 'How\'s the pick hunting going?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28000, 'Taming a Monster'),
(28001, 'Storage Keeper Curly of Uruga asks you to defeat 150 Kart Miners and collect a Cart to move heavy loads. \n(Search Burning Rock. You must defeat 150 Kart Miners to obtain the Cart) \n[LINE] \n[SHOW_REWARD] '),
(28002, 'Hey come on! Get over here! What\'s keeping you kid?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28003, 'What\'s up?\n[NEXT]'),
(28004, 'I got a favor to ask. \nYou know what Kart Miners are right? Those dirty little monster with a cart permanately attached to their hands. \n[NEXT]'),
(28005, 'Yes... why?\n[NEXT]'),
(28006, 'As you probably know, they do have some power to their attacks right? They also have a cart attached to their body! I mean, they\'ll make a great porter don\'t you think? Well I thought you could beat the living daylights out of them and bring {color,yellow,1 Cart} back. \nI just want to see, how their carts are constructed.\n[BUTTON]=[I guess it\'s possible. Sure.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[No way, and also slavery of any kind is horrible.][2]'),
(28007, 'Here Curly, here you go.\nI\'ve got your cart but, I really doubt that you can tame them to do your biddings.\n[NEXT]'),
(28008, 'HAHAHA, I knew it.\nIt\'s fine, I always wanted take a look at that cart anyways.\nHere\'s your reward.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(28009, 'Why don\'t you try to take them on?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28100, 'Light and Shadow Song 1'),
(28101, 'Town Chief Adrian of Uruga asks to speak to you about the origin of this new music spreading throughout the land Isya.\n(Search Uruga)\n(Epic Quest)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(28102, '[NAME]. You came... \n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28103, 'What is it chief? Is everything okay?\nYou don\'t look so good.\n[NEXT]'),
(28104, 'I\'m sorry I don\'t feel so well.\nWell, first thing first. I have to tell you something really important.\n[NEXT]'),
(28105, 'Sure thing. What\'s on your mind?\n[NEXT]'),
(28106, 'First, I want you to know this [NAME], you and I might not share the same opinions.\n[NEXT]'),
(28107, 'Oh.. Okay.\n[NEXT]'),
(28108, 'Could you please listen to the song first?\n{color,yellow,Scorching red river will overflow, rejoicing deadly streams.}\n{color,yellow,It is sorrowful to see breath taken by life is turned to black ashe.}\n{color,yellow,Light turns into 13 pillar and stands against the shadow}\n{color,yellow,One who holds the world in their heart,}\n{color,yellow,will take a stand and won\'t let go.}\n[NEXT]'),
(28109, 'Song of light... I\'ve heard it before. I thought it was a folk song villagers sung. Well, what does the song really represent? What do they mean by 13 pillars?\n[NEXT]'),
(28110, 'Yes, 13 pillars.\nThe song means to protect the pillars.\nThis is song the of shadows.\n{color,yellow,A deadly land overruned by glowing rivers like the deep red dusk.}\n{color,yellow,Run far, far away.}\n{color,yellow,Do not forsake the shadow casted by the sun.}\n{color,yellow,Trusting only what you see, will bring your doom.}\n{color,yellow,The darkness turns into 13 pillars and inroad all lights.}\n[NEXT]'),
(28111, 'Wait a minute... This is... Burning Rock...?\n[NEXT]'),
(28112, 'Yes, that is the pillar.\n[NAME], you have seen it?\nDo you know about a beautifully lit pillar that gleams in transparent glory?\n[NEXT]'),
(28113, 'No one really told me. More like avoided to talk about it.\n[NEXT]'),
(28114, 'That\'s right. The time may have come to tell you about it.\nI need to take a breather.\nCould you ask me about it a bit later?\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(28115, 'Sing for me!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28200, 'A Conversation with Poring '),
(28201, 'Adrian of Uruga would like for you to speak to Poring about the Pillar of Light.                                                 (Epic Quest)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(28202, 'Good, now we can get started.\nI\'m sorry to tell you this but we do not know much about the Light Pillar.\nWe refer to it as a {color,yellow,pillar}. But, {color,yellow,Roumenus} and {color,yellow,new lord of Elderine, Elbama} call it the {color,yellow,Light Pillar}.\n[NEXT]'),
(28203, 'Why is that?\n[NEXT]'),
(28204, 'Perhaps our perceptions of the pillar differ.  Personally, I do not feel any presence of power emitting from it.  \n[NEXT]'),
(28205, 'What do you think it could be? [NEXT]'),
(28206, 'I do not think of it as a divine nor an evil object.  I don\'t have any idea where it came from.  It suddenly appeared one morning in a place where it is impossible to build such a structure.\n[NEXT]'),
(28207, 'I have also seen the pillar.\nI didn\'t sense any special power emitting from it either, however, it was beautiful.  Just looking at it put my mind at peace.\n[NEXT]'),
(28208, 'I do not have any proof that it is of divine nature. \n[NAME], I need to know where this pillar originated from.  Could you find out? You might need to talk to Poring about it.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28209, 'Hey! What is it?\n[NEXT]'),
(28210, 'Do you know anythiing about the \'Light and Shadow Song\'?\n[NEXT]'),
(28211, 'Why of course. I memorized the words.\n[NEXT]'),
(28212, 'Really? Where did you first encounter this song?\n[NEXT]'),
(28213, 'I heard about it from Forrest Tim.  \n[NEXT]'),
(28214, 'Thank you for your help!\nLet\'s go see Tim!\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]'),
(28215, 'I don\'t have a clue who came up with this song actually. \n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28300, 'Meeting Forest Tim'),
(28301, 'Poring of Uruga would like you to speak to Forest Tim.  (Search Uruga) \n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(28302, 'Forest Tim told me about the Light and Shadow Song.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28303, 'Oh hi! It\'s been a while, what brings you here?\n[NEXT]'),
(28304, 'I was wondering if you know anything about the Light and Shadow Song.   \n[NEXT]'),
(28305, 'Mr. Vellon was singing it and it was so engaging that I asked him to teach me. \n[NEXT]'),
(28306, 'Oh I see! Thank you.  I will ask him about the song.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(28307, 'What is it?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28400, 'Talking with Mr. Vellon'),
(28401, 'Forest Tim of Uruga would like you to ask Mr. Vellon about the Light and Shadow Song. (Search Uruga)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(28402, 'You should ask Mr. Vellon about the Light and Shadow Song.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28403, 'Hey!  Good timing!  I just finished a new song!  You have to listen to this.\n[NEXT]'),
(28404, 'Could I hear it later?  Do you know anything about the Light and Shadow Song?  [NEXT]'),
(28405, 'Huh?  Oh!  That song!\nYes, I heard it from a little girl near town.  She definitely wasn\'t a local.  Actually, she was a bit creepy.  She gave me the lyrics and asked me to sing it for her.  So I did.\n[NEXT]'),
(28406, 'I see.  Do you know what she looked like?\n[NEXT]'),
(28407, 'I don\'t know.  I remember the song very well but I can\'t remember her.  Oh!  Curly was there too!  You could ask him if he remembers her.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(28408, 'Did you talk to Curly yet?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28500, 'Talking with Curly'),
(28501, 'Mr. Vellon of Uruga wants you to ask Storage Keeper Curly about the little girl. \n(Search Uruga)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(28502, 'I\'m sure Curly won\'t forget a girl\'s face, if you know what I mean.\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28503, 'Hey what\'s going on? It\'s been a while.\n[NEXT]'),
(28504, 'Yes how are you?  I got a question for you.  \n[NEXT]'),
(28505, 'What is it? \n[NEXT]'),
(28506, 'Do you remember the Light and Shadow Song that you and Mr. Vellon learned from a little girl?\nDo you remember anything about her, like what she looked like or where did she come from?\n[NEXT]'),
(28507, 'Huh?  A little girl?  I don\'t think she was a little girl.  I remember a beautiful woman. \n[NEXT]'),
(28508, '(How did a creepy little girl turn into to a beautiful woman?  Now that\'s creepy.)\nI see... Okay I\'ll be on my way then.\n(I should go back and see Chief Adrian)\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(28509, 'Oh, you\'re back.  You want to listen to my song huh?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28600, 'Returning to Adrian'),
(28601, 'Tell Chief Adrian of Uruga what you\'ve found.\n(Search Uruga)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(28602, 'Hey thanks Curly, I\'ll be on my way then.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28603, 'Chief Adrian!\n[NEXT]'),
(28604, 'Oh! How did it go?\n[NEXT]'),
(28605, 'Well, It\'s a little weird. Both Curly and Vellon swears they learned this song from a girl... but one says it was a little girl and the other says it was a hot lady.  \n[NEXT] '),
(28606, '(Adrian turns pale)\n[NEXT]'),
(28607, 'Hey Adrian! What\'s going on? Adrian wake up!   \n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(28608, 'What\'s the secret behind that song?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28700, 'Light and Shadow Song 2'),
(28701, 'You have to investigate the Light Pillar.  \n(Epic Quest) \n[LINE] \n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(28702, 'Adrian! Wake up!\nCome on Adrian!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28703, 'Oh, I\'m sorry. I would like to rest a little.\n[NAME], Could you do me a favor?\n[NEXT]'),
(28704, 'Sure thing. What is it?\n[NEXT]'),
(28705, 'Could you go investigate the Light Pillar at Burning Rock?\nI\'m sure there is some sort of clue you\'ll discover.\n[BUTTON]=[Sure, I\'ll find out.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I don\'t know it\'s too vague.][2]'),
(28706, 'How are you, Chief?  Take a look at this!  \n[NEXT]'),
(28707, 'This is... \n(A nail-tip sized piece of a gleaming fragment. Adrian is examining it very closely. Then nods her head in conviction)\n[NEXT] '),
(28708, 'Adrian?\n[NEXT]'),
(28709, 'This is a piece of the pillar. [NAME], how did you get this? That pillar is virtually indestructable, no force was ever able to make a scratch on that pillar. I don\'t know how you managed to retrieved this, but I am very grateful. \nCould you please wait a while? I need to assemble an emergency meeting.  After the meeting, I\'ll inform you of our findings.\nFrom the bottom of my heart, thank you.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(28710, 'I am still wondering how did you get that piece off of the pillar.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28800, 'Light and Shadow Song 3'),
(28801, 'Lord Elbama of Elderine has summoned you.  You must deliver the Light Pillar piece to him.  \n(Epic Quest)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(28802, 'Are you [NAME]?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28803, 'Yes, I am. How may I be of service to you?\n[NEXT]'),
(28804, '<Attendant 1>\nHow dare you look straight into Lord Elbama\'s eyes!\n\n<Attendant 2>\nWatch yourself young one, or it\'ll be your last move!\n\n<Lord Elbama>\nAh, ah!\nEnough! \nDear traveler, one that is called [NAME].\nDid you give this Light Pillar fragment to Adrian?\n[NEXT]'),
(28805, '(Wait a minute. Lord Elbama is a mere human.  But he\'s referring chief Adrian by her first name.  I know for a fact that the chief lived for more than 300 years)\nYes that\'s right.\n[NEXT]'),
(28806, '<Attendant 1>\nInsolent fool! Show respect to your lord!\n\n<Lord Elbama>\nI said it\'s fine!\nSo tell me dear traveler. Could you grant me a wish? Could you fetch me a {color,yellow,piece of Light Pillar} as well?\nIt seems only you are able to carry out this duty.\n[BUTTON]=[Why not? Let\'s do it.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Forget it, I\'ll just say that I can\'t.][2]'),
(28807, 'Here it is.\n[NEXT]'),
(28808, 'Thank you. \nYou may be on your way now.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(28809, 'Do you have it yet?\nCan you hurry up?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28900, 'Light and Shadow Song 4'),
(28901, 'Chief Roumenus of Roumen summoned you. You must fetch a Light Pillar piece for Chief Roumenus as well. \n(Epic Quest)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(28902, 'Hey! It\'s been a while. Why don\'t you visit Roumen anymore?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(28903, 'I\'m sorry, I\'ve been busy.\nIs there anything I can do for you?\n[NEXT]'),
(28904, 'Yes, as a matter of fact there is. \nI\'ve heard that you were able to acquire a Light Pillar piece.\n[NEXT]'),
(28905, '(Oh again? Even Chief Roumenus has jumped on the band wagon)\nYes, It seems that way.\n[NEXT]'),
(28906, 'I was wondering if you can get me one too! It\'s very important!\nPlease?\n[BUTTON]=[It\'s Chief Roumenus after all, let\'s do it.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Something fishy is going on.  I don\'t want to be a part of it.][2]'),
(28907, 'Chief, here it is.\n[NEXT]'),
(28908, 'Oh wow! You really did it.\nThat is amazing, you can just take it off like that. That pillar is invincible!\nThank you so much!\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(28909, 'Well be on your way then, go on!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29000, 'Light and Shadow Song 5'),
(29001, 'Listen to Adrian\'s tale about the Light Pillar and the Light and Shadow song.  \n(Epic Quest)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29002, '[NAME]. I have something to tell you. Can you spare some time?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29003, 'Sure, go ahead.\n[NEXT]'),
(29004, '[NAME], please keep an open mind and put your opinions to the side for now.  Please listen to the whole story.\n[NEXT]'),
(29005, '(Okay. I suppose I can...)\nSure.\n[NEXT]'),
(29006, 'Yes that\'s right...\nNow listen carefully.\n\nIf you analyze the Light and Shadow Song, its message is that the: \n{color,yellow,Light Song means to protect the Light Pillar at all costs because it will bring salvation. The Light Pillar is the key to protection from darkness.}\nAnd the{color,yellow,Shadow Song contains the complete opposite message to the Light Song,  It claims that the Light Pillar will only bring evil and destruction to this world.}\n\nWhat do you think, [NAME]? What\'s your opinion on the issue?\n[BUTTON]=[The Light Pillar should be protected.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[We should destroy that deadly Pillar.][2]\n[BUTTON]=[Maybe we should wait before we make any hasty decisions.][3]'),
(29007, 'Protect it? You really think so?\n[NEXT]'),
(29008, 'Did you just say destroy it?\n[NEXT]'),
(29009, 'Observe it?  Let\'s leave it alone you mean.  Right?  \n[NEXT]'),
(29010, 'Now I know how you feel about this issue, [NAME]\nThank you so much for your input.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29011, 'Thank you again for your input.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29100, 'Light and Shadow Song 6'),
(29101, 'Roumenus of Roumen would like to tell you his version.  \n(Epic Quest)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29102, 'Please come in. I\'ve been waiting for you.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29103, 'Did you summon me?\n(He seems worried)\n[NEXT]'),
(29104, 'Well... It\'s not an urgent matter. Why don\'t you have a seat.\n[NEXT]'),
(29105, '(What could it be?)\n[NEXT]'),
(29106, 'Do you remember what I\'ve told you about the birth of Isya long ago?\nAll the history of these continents?\n[NEXT]'),
(29107, 'Yes of course. How can I forget?\n[NEXT]'),
(29108, 'Yes! Good! You remember.\nHmm... I\'ve been thinking a lot lately.\nThe power of light is getting stronger.\nThe power of light from history has defeated darkness and has given birth to peace on this land.  Don\'t you agree?\n[NEXT]'),
(29109, 'Yes, it did. \nHowever, I don\'t think it finished its job.\n[NEXT]'),
(29110, 'You\'re right. However, one can argue that living, breathing and completing daily chores are enough peace for now.\nI really don\'t believe that our lives are in jeopardy, that we will have misery.\nI believe that the power of light can drive off any kind of darkness.\nBeing positive and following the path of light are the powers that can brighten our lives.\n[NEXT]'),
(29111, 'Believe in power of light?\n[NEXT]'),
(29112, 'Yes.  That\'s why I started to believe only in the power of light.  \nWe believed in the light and ran towards it.\nI believe the key to the power of light is that pillar.\nI believe it is the source of power of light that strengthens us.\n[NAME], I want to know where you stand on this issue.\n[BUTTON]=[I believe in the power of light. I agree with you.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[That is the stupidest thing I\'ve ever heard.][2]\n[BUTTON]=[I believe it\'s too early to make a conclusion.][3]'),
(29113, 'Yes! Believing in light is the most important thing.\n[NEXT]'),
(29114, 'You think believing in light is nonsense?\n[NEXT]'),
(29115, 'I see. You haven\'t made a decision yet.\n[NEXT]'),
(29116, 'I see, now I know how you feel about it.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29117, 'Listen.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29200, 'Light and Shadow Song 7'),
(29201, 'You must listen to Lord Elbama\'s thoughts, and voice your opinion. \n(Epic Quest)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29202, '[NAME], you have arrived.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29203, 'Hello Lord Elbama.\nYou summoned me?\n[NEXT]'),
(29204, 'Well... I just have something to ask you.\nI\'ve been hearing about your reputation from the villagers. \n[NEXT]'),
(29205, 'My reputation?\n(For what?)\n[NEXT]'),
(29206, 'I need an opinion from the travelers. \nWhat if, a very beautiful lady suddenly appears in a very horrible place. \nJust suddenly appeared and no one knows where she came from.  She doesn\'t breathe a word about why she has appeared. \nPeople debated over her motives, saying that she brings suffering and evil.  Some say she is the saint here to save us all.  Some say why waste our breathe on such a worthless nobody? \n[NEXT]'),
(29207, 'Did you find out who she was?\n[NEXT]'),
(29208, 'To this day, no one really knows...\nEven those with great knowledge do not know anything about her.\nWhat do you think about such a person?\n[BUTTON]=[Seed of destruction of course.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[A saint, what else?][2]\n[BUTTON]=[I don\'t know, I don\'t think she\'s anybody special.][3]'),
(29209, 'A seed of destruction? But she hasn\'t done anything...\n[NEXT]'),
(29210, 'A saint? But we don\'t know anything about her...\n[NEXT]'),
(29211, 'Hmm... nobody special...\n[NEXT]'),
(29212, 'I see now...\nYou may go now.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29213, 'Why don\'t you listen to the whole story?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29300, 'Light and Shadow Song 8'),
(29301, 'You must speak to Chief Adrian of Uruga. \n(Epic quest)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29302, 'Chief Adrian?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29303, '[NAME]! what brings you here?\n[NEXT]'),
(29304, '(Why is she so surprised to see me?)\nUmm... I have some issues that I would like to discuss with you.\n[NEXT]'),
(29305, 'Yes, go ahead. What\'s on your mind?\n[NEXT]'),
(29306, 'Well, Chief Roumenus, Lord Elbama and others have been asking me a lot of weird questions.  I just wanted to know why they are asking me?\n[NEXT]'),
(29307, 'I see. So they were asking questions as well?\n[NEXT]'),
(29308, 'Can you tell me what\'s going on?\nPlease?\n[NEXT]'),
(29309, 'I apologize for any worry we might have caused you, [NAME].\nI\'ll tell you what\'s going on.\nA few days ago, I called for a meeting.  It was about the pillar and its existence. \nWe already know about our stands on the matter.  So we wanted to have a meeting and discuss it further.  \nHowever, the meeting was cancelled by Lord Elbama. \n[NEXT]'),
(29310, 'Why? Did he give a reason?\n[NEXT]'),
(29311, 'I do have a theory about why he cancelled, but I don\'t think it\'s ethical to just tell you my speculation. \nIf we did hold a meeting, it would\'ve been a first time for him to attend such an important meeting. \nHe\'s fairly new to his job, and before he came aboard, Captain Shutian looked after the city of Elderine.  Before Elbama became our Lord, he was a high priest.  It\'s only been two years since he has taken over.\n[NEXT]'),
(29312, 'I haven\'t seen him before either. \nNo one really knew anything about him.\nHow did he attain such a position?\n[NEXT]'),
(29313, 'I don\'t think it\'s time yet to discuss such issues.\nI still have faith.\nWhen it is finally revealed. I\'ll tell you then.\nI am truly sorry, [NAME]. I sincerely apologize.\n[NEXT]'),
(29314, 'No not at all.\nBut please tell me when you\'re ready.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29315, 'Please be patient [NAME]\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29400, 'Light and Shadow Song 9'),
(29401, 'Please bring a Light Pillar piece to Albert Galdaras and answer his questions as well.  [LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]   '),
(29402, 'Hey over here.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29403, 'Hello Mr. Albert, Galdaras, and... \n[NEXT]'),
(29404, 'Oh no need to be so formal, just call me Ed.\n[NEXT]'),
(29405, 'Oh Ed! What can I do for you?\n[NEXT]'),
(29406, 'Oh I\'m sure you already know what I\'m about to ask you. I mean... Come on right?\n[NEXT]'),
(29407, 'Ask me what?\n[NEXT]'),
(29408, 'Hey, stop playing around!  I\'m on your side!  There\'s a weird mood going on in the town.  Don\'t think your efforts are going unnoticed!\n[NEXT]'),
(29409, '...\n(Somber)\n[NEXT]'),
(29410, 'Cheer up!  It was inevitable after all.  If you can\'t do it, no one can.  None of this is your fault.\n[NEXT]'),
(29411, 'I am worried that my answers are the cause of this somber mood and division amongst friends around town just because of that pillar.  It really makes me sad to see it.\n[NEXT]'),
(29412, 'That isn\'t your fault.  It is in our nature to disagree.  However, it is also in our duty to find out the truth. \nI was wondering, if you could do me a favor and bring me a piece of that Light Pillar. \n[BUTTON]=[Huh? Oh okay.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[What?  So you can jump on the bandwagon too?  NO!][2]\n'),
(29413, 'Ed, here it is...\n[NEXT]'),
(29414, 'Good.\nLook carefully.\n(FLASH!)\n[NEXT]'),
(29415, '(The piece is glowing in Ed\'s hand)\nWhat! Hey! How did you do that?\n(The piece disintegrates into fine dust. A trace of light glittered as it fell from Ed\'s fist)\n[NEXT]'),
(29416, 'Did you see?\nIts nothing really.\nIt isn\'t the light, darkness, nor meaningless. \nWhat do you suppose it is then?\n[NEXT]'),
(29417, ' I really don\'t know.\n[NEXT]'),
(29418, 'This is...\n\n{color,yellow,Chaos}\n\nThat is the true nature of the \'Pillar\'.\nA meaningless object shaking the foundation of faith, stomping on order, and causing conflict.\nThis seed of conflict is probably someone\'s plot. \nNo wonder you\'ve been hurt in the process, you were pulled in so many directions.\n[NEXT]'),
(29419, 'I thought that there isn\'t a clear answer! You can\'t just take a side!\n[NEXT]'),
(29420, 'No, \nIf you believe in something, then you must only look towards your truth and believe it with your life.\n{color,yellow,[NAME]}\n{color,yellow,There isn\'t just one truth in this world.}\nI\'m not sure this will sink in, but in the future you will realize what is at stake.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete epic quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29421, 'Did that help you at all?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29422, 'Examine the Light Pillar'),
(29423, 'Take a close look at the Light Pillar in Burning Rock and retrieve another sample.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29424, 'It is an amazing pillar. Wow!\n(Examine carefully)\n[NEXT]'),
(29425, 'It is pretty hard.\n(Tampering with the pillar\'s surface)\nIt sure looks transparent from outside.\n[NEXT]'),
(29426, 'Wait, there is a hairline fracture.\nMaybe I could loosen it.\n[NEXT]'),
(29600, 'Maria\'s Tear 1'),
(29601, 'Maria from Roumen is upset that she can\'t get in contact with Elderine Item Merchant Kenton. \nLet\'s get 30 Red Nix\'s meat for Maria\'s orphans.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29602, '[NAME]. [NAME].\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29603, 'Hey Maria, how have you been?\n[NEXT]'),
(29604, 'I have a favor to ask you.\nWell, Mr. Kenton from Elderine has been a big contributor to our orphanage, but lately I can\'t get in touch with him.\nI am very worried.\nOur kids have been starving for the past few days, eating watered down potato soup.  So I was wondering if you could get some Red Nix meat for the children. About 30 Red Nix meat will do.\n[BUTTON]=[Sure thing, don\'t worry about it.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I can\'t, I\'m starving too you know.][2]'),
(29605, 'Maria, so did you get in touch with Kenton yet?\n[NEXT]'),
(29606, 'No... not yet.\nOh, I forgot to tell you how  much I appreciate your help.\nI\'ll try to take care of the rest some how.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29607, 'Please hurry!  The children are starving.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29700, 'Maria\'s Tear 2'),
(29701, 'Maria from Roumen received a letter from Kenton, which states that he can no longer help out with the orphanage contribution. \nYou must bring Low SP potion for Maria and 20 Red Nix Meats, 40 Mushrooms, and 10 Geraniums for the starving children.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29702, 'Maria, what\'s wrong? Why are you crying?\nAre you okay?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29703, 'Oh, I\'m sorry.\n[NEXT]'),
(29704, 'But you are crying! Tell me what\'s going on?\n[NEXT]'),
(29705, 'I received a letter from Kenton.\nHe said that he can\'t contribute anymore and tells me to find other contributors from now on.\nThe children are so malnourished that they can\'t even play anymore.  I\'ve asked the Chief to help, but the town is in its greatest recession ever.  No time for tears.  I\'m sorry but I must be on my way, I need to get some food and herbs for the children. \n[BUTTON]=[Wait, I\'ll go in your place.  Just hang on.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Yes tough luck.  See you later.][2]'),
(29706, 'Maria! Here take this.  I got some food, herbs, and SP potion for you.\n[NEXT]'),
(29707, 'Thank you.\nI am in your debt.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29708, 'The poor children!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29800, 'Kenton\'s Excuses'),
(29801, 'Kenton wants to explain why he couldn\'t help out the orphanage anymore.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29802, '[NAME]?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29803, 'Kenton?\n(Hey, he seems to be his usual self. I should ask about Maria\'s situation)\n[NEXT]'),
(29804, 'Did... Did Maria... Say anything?\n[NEXT]'),
(29805, 'Yes, as a matter of fact...\nHOW COULD YOU!!!\nI am SO disappointed in YOU!\nI thought you were a good person regardless of all those ridiculous glamour wannabe looks.  But I guess your inside now matches the outside, doesn\'t it!?\n[NEXT]'),
(29806, 'You got me all wrong!  That\'s not the whole story really!  You know, an elegant person like me shouldn\'t be explaining myself.  Just listen.\nThere was a reason why I couldn\'t help Maria out.  As you probably know, I was in charge of collecting the orphanage contributions.  But while we were having a meeting, the committee had a big fight on where and how the contributions should be spent! \nThe committee was asking why are we helping other towns\' facilities when our own town\'s orphanage is in a rut?\nSo all the funding to Roumen\'s orphanage was cut.\nThe whole town is in a recession and everyone is a bit edgy.\n[NEXT]'),
(29807, 'You are saying that when it gets tough, you can\'t help the ones who need the most?\nYou\'re selfish.  That is what it sounds like.\n[NEXT]'),
(29808, 'We are in big financial trouble you know.\n[NEXT]'),
(29809, 'It doesn\'t matter.\nThose children will go hungry.\nI thought, if your town committee would not help, at least you\'ll do something about your commitment regardless. I can\'t say that I\'m not disappointed. \nIt\'s just too sad to see those kids starve.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29810, 'Well... That\'s... You see...\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29900, 'Lies 1'),
(29901, 'Uruga town\'s Blacksmith Hans is suffering from a  shortage of materials for his foundary. You must lie to Roumen\'s Blacksmith James in order to help Hans. \n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29902, '[NAME]!! Oh great!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29903, 'What are you up to?\n[NEXT]'),
(29904, 'Wow you are good!  Are you psychic?\nI desperately need your help! I am in need of Silver, and Mithril ores. It\'s really scarce here at Uruga or Elderine, but at Roumen, there are a ton of them!  So, I sent a letter to Roumen to request the ore.  But... the letter was returned to me unopened.  He\'s making a clear statement that he doesn\'t want to deal with me.\nCould you please could get it for me?  \n[NEXT]'),
(29905, 'Are you asking me to lie?\n[NEXT]'),
(29906, 'Well, it\'s for a noble cause and you also refine ore from time to time.  I know he won\'t suspect a thing.  So please do this for me.\n[BUTTON]=[I guess so.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[NO WAY!][2]'),
(29907, 'James...\nHey! What\'s going on? I have a favor to ask you.\nI\'m kind of into making a weapon and I need some Silver and Mithril ores. \nOf course I\'ll pay.\n[NEXT]'),
(29908, 'WHAT DO YOU TAKE ME FOR?\nDON\'T TRY TO FOOL ME!  YOU WERE SENT BY THOSE URUGA FOLK!  WEREN\'T YOU?!  LOOK INTO MY EYES AND SAY THAT AGAIN!\n[NEXT]'),
(29909, '(How did he know?)\nI\'m sorry!  I didn\'t mean to lie!  I was only trying to help.\n[NEXT]'),
(29910, 'Hmph!  No way in a hell I\'ll help those selfish, ungrateful people!  Do you think I\'ll help those folks who\'d rather see Roumen\'s orphans go hungry?  HA!  GET LOST!\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29911, 'Did you get it?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30000, 'Lies 2'),
(30001, 'You must tell Hans about James\' reaction.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30002, 'Oh, good.  You\'re back! \n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30003, 'Hans...\n[NEXT]'),
(30004, 'Oh! So, how did it go? Did you get it?\n[NEXT]'),
(30005, 'Well, no...\nHe didn\'t buy it.\n[NEXT]'),
(30006, 'I kind of suspected but I thought James would listen to your plea.\nI suppose it was useless.\nI have no choice but to cancel all incoming orders.  I just simply can\'t run a store without raw materials. I guess in a way it is poetic justice.  We didn\'t help Roumen when they needed help.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30007, 'Hmph! \n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30100, 'Meeting my fiancee shouldn\'t be this hard!'),
(30101, 'Elderine\'s Storage Keeper Kyle is having a hard time meeting with his fiancee.  You must bring him 3 Crystal Guardian Cores to help out with his rendezvous.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30102, '[NAME]! Hey [NAME]!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30103, 'Hey Kyle, how have you been?\nHow\'s your love life going?\n[NEXT]'),
(30104, 'Problem is that IT\'S NOT GOING AT ALL! I am so frustrated!!!\n[NEXT]'),
(30105, 'What happened?\n[NEXT]'),
(30106, 'Well, my fiancee moved to Roumen recently.\nAnd you know how our towns\' relationship with Roumen is so sour these days. Recently, we can\'t even meet up for dates.\nHer father is also saying things like if I don\'t becme a part of Roumen, I can forget about the wedding.\nWe were going to meet up tonight like a pair of star crossed lovers, but the path to Roumen isn\'t so safe.  Maybe you can get me some Crystal Guardian Cores?  Then I should be able to light up the path so that is safe enough for me to travel! I know that I\'m asking too much.\n[BUTTON]=[For love, I\'ll do anything.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Are you insane? No way!][2]'),
(30107, 'Okay, Whew! Here take it.\n[NEXT]'),
(30108, 'Oh thank you! Thanks to you I will be able to meet with my lady!  Thank you for your trouble.\nAll this drama between our towns are killing me.  Why can\'t we just get along?\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30109, 'Please, I\'m counting on you!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30200, 'Lava ViVi\'s Spark'),
(30201, 'Storage Keeper Curly of Uruga wants to add Lava ViVi\'s spark to his collection.\nPlease bring Curly 5 Lava ViVi\'s Flames.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30202, 'Hey! Good to see you! Welcome!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30203, 'Hey, Curly.  What\'s going on?\n[NEXT]'),
(30204, 'HAHAHA! Well, I have a collection that I\'m dying to possess. \nMy ViVi set is almost complete! Only thing missing is a Lava ViVi\'s flame.  There simply wasn\'t anyone strong enough to fetch them, but I think maybe you are. What do you say?\n[NEXT]'),
(30205, 'Okay fine! You want Lava ViVi\'s flame right? How do I transport them?\n[NEXT]'),
(30206, 'When you pick them up, occasionally they drop a spark that has been solidified.  It is a rare find and because of that, it is expensive.  You won\'t be disappointed with the reward.\n[BUTTON]=[Okay, it better be good.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I don\'t want to do it.][2]'),
(30207, 'That wasn\'t fun at all.  Look at these burns!  Here, Curly.\nYou get my reward?\n[NEXT]'),
(30208, 'I thought you could handle some heat!  Don\'t make such a fuss! \nI finally get to possess such a beautiful speciman!  Thank you! \n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30209, 'It has such beautiful flames!  One cannot compare such beauty.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30300, 'A Jewel Tree'),
(30301, 'Stone Merchant Thompson of Burning Rock has heard of a tree that bares jewels.\nThe Jewel Tree is also in Burning Rock.  You must reveal its true nature to him, and retrieve the fake jewels it produces.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30302, 'Hey over here! Get over here quick!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30303, 'Hey you! What\'s going on?\n[NEXT]'),
(30304, 'What\'s with the attitude? \nAnyway,  I heard this incredible news!  Did you ever hear of anything called a Jewel Tree?  It is rumored to bear jewels like a fruit!\n[NEXT]'),
(30305, 'What about it?\n[NEXT]'),
(30306, 'What\'s wrong with you kid? Didn\'t you hear me?  I said a tree that bares JEWELS!\nIt isn\'t just any tree!  Do you want to become partners?  You provide me those jewels and I\'ll sell it for a large profit!  How about it?\n[BUTTON]=[Those are fakes, fine I\'ll get them and you can see it for yourself!][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Get them yourself.[2]'),
(30307, 'See?  They\'re fake. \n(The sparkling jewels turn to ash as you present them to him.)\n[NEXT]'),
(30308, 'Huh?  This can\'t be!  Why is this happening?\nYou are trying to con me, huh?  So you can have it all to yourself!  You should\'ve just said no if you didn\'t want to do it! \n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30309, 'So what are you going to show me?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30400, 'Maxuter\'s Request 1'),
(30401, 'Maxouter of Burning Rock asks you to retrieve 30 Hot Stones from Magmatons.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30402, 'Hello.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30403, 'Hello, Maxouter.\nThe scorching red sky of Burning Rock always amazes me.\n[NEXT]'),
(30404, 'Yes, I agree. This red sky is one of a kind. \nI was wondering if I could ask a favor of you.  There is a request I think you are able to take on.  Are you interested?\n[NEXT]'),
(30405, 'Yes! I am. What is it?\n[NEXT]'),
(30406, 'Oh good, thank you.\nIt seems that they are putting in a new radiant heating floor for the senior center in town. So this request for Magmaton stones came in, saying it makes a superb heating surface. \nMay I trouble you for {color,yellow,30 of Magmaton\'s Hot Stones}?\n[BUTTON]=[Sure thing!][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Magmaton? Maybe next time... ][2]'),
(30407, 'Whoa, hot! So hot! Here you go Maxuter.\n[NEXT]'),
(30408, 'WHOA! OUCH! SO HOT!\nAh! HA HA HA! I\'m sorry to display such an undignifed spectacle.\nHere\'s your reward. Thank you.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30409, 'Please take care of yourself.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30500, 'Maxuter\'s Request 2'),
(30501, 'You have received another request from Maxouter of Burning Rock\nYou must hunt Flame Moles and retrieve 35 Mole Masks. \n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30502, 'Maxouter, did another request come in?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30503, 'There you are! Yes, as a matter of fact.\nThis time it\'s a gas mask for experiments. \nCould I trouble you for 35 Mole Masks?\n[BUTTON]=[Yes, I\'ll be back][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Ooh ... I have a sudden back pain][2]'),
(30504, 'Here! It\'s one funny looking mask.\n[NEXT]'),
(30505, 'Yes it is.\nHere\'s your reward. Thank you.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30506, 'You should be able to find Flame Moles at the Flaming Mine.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30600, 'Red Feathers'),
(30601, 'Vegan Goblin is madly in love these days.\nYou must get 40 red feathers for his girl friend Malabutia.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30602, 'Hey, [NAME]! \n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30603, 'Hey! What\'s going on?\nWhy are you blushing?\n[NEXT]'),
(30604, 'Ho Ho, I AM IN A RELATIONSHIP!!!\n[NEXT]'),
(30605, 'Whoa! Really? With Malabutia? Good for you! But isn\'t she a full blown carnivore? How\'s that working out for you?\n[NEXT]'),
(30606, 'Love will conqure all! HOHOHOHO!\nBesides, I can compensate for my flaws with crazy gifts!  I\'m not worried at all.  I mean I have you, [NAME].  You always help out with getting gifts and such.  It\'s a win-win situation for me!  Speaking of which, you know about Red Nixes right?  I\'m thinking of making one hot red feather head piece for her.  Can you get me 40 red feathers from Red Nixes? \n[BUTTON]=[Okay, but it ain\'t free, so get your money ready!][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I don\'t know what Red Nixes are.][2]'),
(30607, 'Alright man, count\'em!  40 Red Nix feathers! Where\'s my reward?\n[NEXT]'),
(30608, 'Whoa! Look at that red passionate color! It looks like a crosscut view of my buring passion for her! Thank you! Thank you so so much!\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30609, 'You want some mushrooms? I\'ve got plenty.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30700, 'Cooled off Heating Stones'),
(30701, 'Blacksmith Hans of Uruga is asking that you gather 35 Lava Magmaton\'s very hot stones so he can make a radiant heating surface for his aunt and grandmother.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30702, 'There you are! Good timing, I got something to ask you.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30703, 'Sure, what\'s going on? Hey! That was a hot stone I got for Maxuter! \n[NEXT]'),
(30704, 'Yes that\'s right.  I put in that request.  It was for my aunt and my grandmother. Only thing was that the hot stones you got from the Magmaton weren\'t hot enough.  I was thinking, If we use Lava Magmaton, it\'ll be hot enough and will last longer.\n[NEXT]'),
(30705, 'All transactions are final. I don\'t give warranties. \n[NEXT]'),
(30706, 'Hey, hey, don\'t worry... What do you take me for? I\'ll pay of course. Don\'t worry about it. So can you get me {color,yellow,35} of those {color,yellow,Very Hot Stones}? \n[BUTTON]=[Just get your money ready! I\'ll be back.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[No way, you cheapskate!][2]'),
(30707, 'Whoaaaa, soooooo hot! Here! Take it!\n[NEXT]'),
(30708, 'Hey! Watch it! Don\'t throw them around!\nI almost got burned.\nHere, take your reward.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30709, 'Hey come back quick.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30800, 'Man-Eater 1'),
(30801, 'Adrian from Uruga is asking you to hunt down 150 man-eating Lava Gargoyles who ate 8 villagers. \n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30802, 'Sobs... \n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30803, 'Adrian? What\'s going on? Why are you crying?\n(She doesn\'t seem like the crying type.)\n[NEXT]'),
(30804, 'My apologies to show such weakness.\nIt\'s just too sad to see.\nI\'m alright now.  Lately there have been too many tragic events occuring around town, that I can\'t even sleep at night.\n[NEXT]'),
(30805, 'You are right. It seems like bad events keep happening one after another.\nWhat happened?  \n[NEXT]'),
(30806, '6 villagers and 2 travelers were eaten by the Lava Gargoyles. According to the witnesses, they were attacked by a group of Lava Gargoyles near Burning Rock. It happened so fast that the victims didn\'t even have time to scream. \nVictims include my godson whom I personally named. Killing 150 Lava Gargoyles will put their souls at rest.\n[BUTTON]=[Don\'t worry, I\'ll get them.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Too bad. So sad. I\'ll send some flowers.][2]'),
(30807, 'Adrian! I got\'em. Every single one of them.\nI hope it helped.\n[NEXT]'),
(30808, 'I know this won\'t change a thing but now their souls will be at peace, thanks to you, [NAME].\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30809, '(Sobbing)\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30900, 'Man-Eater 2'),
(30901, 'Adrian from Uruga is asking you to retrieve the last articles left by the victims of the man-eating Lava Gargoyles.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30902, '[NAME]... \n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(30903, 'Yes Adrian.  Are you alright?  How can I help you?\n[NEXT]'),
(30904, 'I\'m alright considering ... but it\'s the families of the victims that I\'m worried about.  I was wondering if you could retrieve the victims\' belongings. \n[NEXT]'),
(30905, 'I see...\n[NEXT]'),
(30906, 'Yes, I thought that at least with their belongings, the victims\' families can have proper burials. \nPlease find their articles.\n[BUTTON]=[Of course, I\'ll be back.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[What? Revenge isn\'t enough? Come on! No.][2]'),
(30907, 'I couldn\'t find all of them but, I was able to retrieve a few.\n[NEXT]'),
(30908, 'Thank you [NAME].  At least their families can have a memorial service. \n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(30909, 'This is really tragic.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29500, 'Vegan Goblin 1'),
(29501, 'Vegan Goblin in Goblin Camp asks you to collect Soft Goblin Mushrooms and Spoiled Mushrooms.\n(Search Goblin Camp. Soft Goblin Mushrooms and Spoiled Mushrooms can be gathered from Mushrooms)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29502, 'Yo! How ya doin\'? Wait Wait!!!\nChill out player I got no beef with you.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(29503, 'Are you saying you aren\'t going to attack me? But don\'t Goblins usually...\n[NEXT]'),
(29504, 'Listen to yourself... \nPrejudice, only brings irate and irate only brings hate!\nDon\'t be a hater kid, do I looks like type of dude that will eat you?\n[NEXT]'),
(29505, 'Well you kind of do...\nBut I got to say, this is first time that I talk to goblin this long before drawing weapons.\n[NEXT]'),
(29506, 'Yes, I\'m telling you not all goblins are fighters some of us, like myself are lovers.\nFor example, I try to apply my love for all life to my everyday life, so I am fully pledged practicing Vegan! These sharp teeth only represent my origin, just the show! I detest any violence.\n[NEXT]'),
(29507, 'I see...\nOkay, I\'m sorry that I try to take you down.\n[NEXT]'),
(29508, 'Apologies accepted.\nHey since we are in an apologetic mood, could you do me a favor? I\'ve been starving for few days and also because of my choice, other goblins are mean to me. Everytime I try to harvest some mushroom to eat, they attack me. So could you possibly get some food for me? I think {color,yellow, Soft Goblin Mushroom} and {color,yellow, Spoiled Mushrooms} will do. Please?\n[BUTTON]=[Alright dude, hang on okay.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Forget it goblin is goblin afterall!][2]'),
(29509, 'Hey, here\'s your mushrooms.\n[NEXT]'),
(29510, 'Thanks! Thanks a lot! I was soooooo hungry that, I was about to faint. I really don\'t know how thank you. Ah! Yes! Take this I made it myself. {color,yellow,It doesn\'t look much, but It\'ll come in handy one day.}\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(29511, 'Oh man... I think my stomach is eating itself. Huh? Why are you looking at me like that? I detest meats!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31000, 'Vegan Goblin 2'),
(31001, 'Vegan Goblin in Goblin Camp asks you to collect Soft Goblin Mushrooms, and of Plain Toadstool.\n(Search Goblin Camp. Soft Goblin Mushrooms, andPlain Toadstool can be gathered from Mushrooms)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31002, '[NAME]...[NAME]... \n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31003, 'Who\'s calling me? Huh? Hey wait a minute, it\'s that timid goblin.\n[NEXT]'),
(31004, 'Timid? Who you calling a timid? Huh?!\n[NEXT]'),
(31005, 'Hey, come down. Do you understand the concept of \'I\'m playin\'? What a drama queen. Well, anyways what\'s up? What does big, bad goblin want from little \'ol me?\n[NEXT]'),
(31006, 'I\'m hungry again... \n[NEXT]'),
(31007, 'Lemme guess, you want me to get some mushroom for your lazy behind.\n[NEXT]'),
(31008, 'Yes! How did you know? You must be like a psychic or something? Have you thought of opening your own 1 900 number? Ha Ha, could you be a dear and get me {color,yellow, Soft Goblin Mushrooms} and {color,yellow, Plain Toadstool}? \n[BUTTON]=[Sure, I\'ll get them for you, and I hope you choke on them.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[You are giving the other goblins a bad name! Get it yourself you filthy monster!][2]'),
(31009, 'Here you go. You\'ll be set for while with these.\n[NEXT]'),
(31010, 'Thanks a lot player! This will be big step towards a good cause. Here kid, I got something for you. Take this.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31011, 'Sky is turning yellow, I\'m so hungry that you look like a mushroom.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31100, 'I Need a Doll! 1'),
(31101, 'Kid Woz in Elderine asks you to speak with im about  picking out a gift for his girlfriend.\n(Search Elderine)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31102, '[NAME]! [NAME]!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31103, 'Woz! Hey how are you doing kid?\n[NEXT]'),
(31104, 'Good it is you! I got a problem. And I really think you are the only one who can help me out.\n[NEXT]'),
(31105, 'You sure? Alright, what is it?\n[NEXT]'),
(31106, 'You know that hottie Pey right? Well Pey have a really cute sister named Patty. She and I decided to go out and go study. UHer birthday is around the corner and I really haven\'t got a clue what to get her. \n[BUTTON]=[What about something to eat? Candy perheps?][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Nothing says I love you more then a cute doll][2]\n[BUTTON]=[Gift? Be a man you should be gift enough.][3]\n[BUTTON]=[I want a gift too.][4]\n[BUTTON]=[Aren\'t you too bit too young to have a relationship?][5]'),
(31107, 'Candy? Pey told me not to get her anything that\'s too sweets.\nCavities...\n[NEXT]'),
(31108, 'Cute dolls! Yes that\'s it! \n[NEXT]'),
(31109, 'What are you talking about?\n[NEXT]'),
(31110, 'Wake up!\n[NEXT]'),
(31111, 'Hey, age is nothing but a number!\n[NEXT]'),
(31112, 'Did you decide what to get her? Doll huh? Good choice.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31113, 'Doll... What type of dolls? So many choices... Yet I draw blank...\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31200, 'I Need a Doll! 2'),
(31201, 'Kid Woz in Elderine asks you to deliver a Doll to his girlfriend.\n(Search Elderine)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31202, 'Sighs...\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31203, 'Hey Woz, what\'s going on? Aren\'t you too young to be sighing like a romantic comedy movie character? \n[NEXT]'),
(31204, 'You remember about my girl friend\'s gift?\n[NEXT]'),
(31205, 'For Patty right?\n[NEXT]'),
(31206, 'Yes... I\'ve been searching everywhere for that special doll... I heard that she is fond of cute monster dolls. But all the dolls I\'m running into are like fashion doll crap! \n[BUTTON]=[Monster doll? Hey how about a Goblin Doll? I happened to have one.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Yo I think she\'s a freak. Girl who likes a monster doll?][2]'),
(31207, 'Here you go Wuz. Goblin Doll. Hope she like it.\n[NEXT]'),
(31208, 'Thanks! Patty will love this for sure!\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31209, 'Umm?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue[1]\n[MENU]'),
(31300, 'Undercover Goblin 1'),
(31301, 'Goblin in Goblin Camp asks you to defeat Goblin Captains in order to infiltrate underground goblin ring.\n(Search Goblin Camp)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31302, 'Shoosh! Be quiet, and don\'t blow my cover!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31303, 'Wait a minute, you are a human!\n[NEXT]'),
(31304, 'Yes, I\'m Agent A. Could you please act natural.\n[NEXT]'),
(31305, 'What are you doing here, looking like that? And how did you able turn yourself like a...\n[NEXT]'),
(31306, 'Goblin? I took a transformation potion, Avon made for me. You look like an able traveler. How about it? Can you defeat {color,yellow, Goblin Captains}? \n[BUTTON]=[Of course, that\'s nothing.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Me? No way.][2]'),
(31307, 'Hey I\'m back. You sure that\'s a disguise? I mean, maybe you do really looks like a...\n[NEXT]'),
(31308, 'Goblin? Hey watch it, if you don\'t want to be an undercover food for an undercover goblin! \n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31309, 'Hey which part of undercover work you don\'t understand? Would you please act natural?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31400, 'Undercover Goblin 2'),
(31401, 'Goblin in Goblin Camp asks you to defeat Goblin Captains and collect explosives.\n(Search Goblin Camp. Explosives can be obtained by defeating Goblin Captains)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31402, 'Hey kid over here.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31403, 'Now what does he want?\n[NEXT]'),
(31404, 'What I want is your loyalty to good cause! There\'s an order from Elderine. We need to set an explosive at Goblin Camp.\n[NEXT]'),
(31405, 'We? Since when?\n[NEXT]'),
(31406, 'Since, I will be paying for your service rendered. Why? Isn\'t that how it goes? Come on, you\'ll get paid and also you\'ll be doing a great service to a mankind. \nGo and defeat {color,yellow, Goblin Captains} and collect {color,yellow, Explosives}.\n[BUTTON]=[Fine, as long as you pay.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Ha! I don\'t think you can afford my services!][2]'),
(31407, 'I did it.\n[NEXT]'),
(31408, 'Good job. Now stay back and don\'t get in the way.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31409, 'What\'s keeping you? Go take them out!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31500, 'Blue Hides from Harken'),
(31501, 'Item Merchant Kenton asks you to collect Harken\'s hides.\n(Search Collapsed Prison)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31502, 'Isn\'t this just dreamy... \n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31503, 'What are you up to?\nWhat\'s with that piece of blue leather?\n[NEXT]'),
(31504, 'It\'s a swatch of leather. Have you seen such beautiful blue leathers before?\n[NEXT]'),
(31505, 'Wait I know that color.\n[NEXT]'),
(31506, 'I\'m sure you\'ve seen it before. It\'s a Harken\'s hide. Cool huh?\nCould you get me {color,yellow, Harken\'s Hides}? I\'m going to make a new collection.\n[BUTTON]=[As long as you pay sure.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[What\'s next, Cubism? Forget it.][2]'),
(31507, 'Here it is. Your start of blue period.\n[NEXT]'),
(31508, 'Are you being sarcastic? These will be the bases of great art. Now be on your way then. I am in no mood to chat up with helps. \n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31509, 'Lalalala Lalalala! Roo roo roo la la la!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31600, 'Weak Ogre\'s Tonic'),
(31601, 'Healer Avon of Elderine asks you to speak to him about a weird tonic was dropped while battling with Weak Ogres. \n(Search Elderine)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31602, 'Hey Avon! Avon! \n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31603, '[NAME], how have you been? It\'s been awhile no?\n[NEXT]'),
(31604, 'A bit. Anyways, I got this while battling with orges. Looks like a medicine.\n[NEXT]'),
(31605, 'Why it is. I believe it\'s a suppliments those Weak Orges take. Let\'s see what\'s in them shell we?\n[NEXT]'),
(31606, 'What kind is it?\n[NEXT]'),
(31607, 'It\'s a revitalizer. \nI suppose they take this to get their strength back. It\'s ingredients are bit perculiar. It\'s feminine for ogre revitalizer. Violet, Geranium, Mushrooms, Flower Petals, Honey... \n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31608, 'Yes?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31700, 'Tonic Research'),
(31701, 'Healer Avon of Elderine asks you to collect Tonics, Violets, Geraniums, Flower Petals, and Honey. \n(Search Collapsed Prison. Tonics, Violets, Geraniums, Flower Petals, and Honey can be obtained by defeating Weakened Ogres) \n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31702, 'It\'s very peculiar.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31703, 'Avon! What\'s going on?\n[NEXT]'),
(31704, 'I\'ve been researching deeper into that tonic you fetched me. I\'ve been cross researching with other ingredients and I think I may have found a really good potion recipe. I want to study further into it, but I may have hit a snag. I need more ingredients. Could you get me more of these tonics? {color,yellow, Tonics}, {color,yellow, Violets}, {color,yellow, Geraniums}, {color,yellow, Flower Petals}, and {color,yellow, Honey} please? It\'ll help out a lot. I believe you can acquire Honey and Flower Petals from flowers. \n[BUTTON]=[Wait, let me jog it down. Okay, sure.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Umm... No.][2]'),
(31705, 'I\'m so tired.\nAvon, I got those ingredients you wanted.\n[NEXT]'),
(31706, 'Thank you. I know it wasn\'t an easy task. Take this for your trouble.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31707, 'How is it going?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31800, 'Traces of Beasts 1'),
(31801, 'Guard Captain Shutian of Elderine asks you to defeat King Colls.\n(Search Collapsed Prison)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31802, '<Guard 1>\nUrgh! My back... It HURTS!\n<Guard 2>\nMy LEGS!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31803, '(What\'s this commotion all about?)\nCaptain Shutian, what\'s going on?\nThese wounded soldiers... what happened?\n[NEXT]'),
(31804, 'Oh you are here.\nYes, broken legs, whiplashes, injured backs. It isn\'t the wounds acquired from monster, but injuries from falling into holes.\n[NEXT]'),
(31805, 'Falling into holes?\n[NEXT]'),
(31806, 'Correct.\nIts how King Colls mark their territory. By digging deep holes everywhere. That is how they catch their prey. However, soldiers on patrol often fall into the holes. \nLately, it\'s just been too much. We need to keep them in check. Could you help me defeat {color,yellow, King Colls}?\n[BUTTON]=[Of course. Leave it to me.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Come on, like you said it\'s in their nature. Leave them be.][2]'),
(31807, 'I\'m back Captain.\n[NEXT]'),
(31808, 'Good job. My men are taking care of those dangerous holes. \n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31809, 'Those holes are making patrol difficult.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31900, 'Traces of Beasts 2'),
(31901, 'Guard Captain Shutian of Elderine and collect King Coll Claws.\n(Search Collapsed Prison. King Coll Claws can be obtained by defeating King Colls)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31902, 'Captain, I haven\'t seen a King Coll holes lately.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(31903, 'Thanks to your hard work.\nThere still is an unfinished issue though. We are thinking of leaving a warning message to those King Colls, by scattering some King Coll claws. That ought a teach them away.\n[NEXT]'),
(31904, 'You think it\'ll work?\n[NEXT]'),
(31905, 'I\'m sure of it. Would you think twice if there are severed fingers scattered all over the place? Do you think you can collect {color,yellow, King Coll Claws} for me?\n[BUTTON]=[You know, I guess so. I\'ll be back.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Severed fingers? Nah.][2]'),
(31906, 'Captain! I\'ve brought back claws.\n[NEXT]'),
(31907, 'You are fast! Amazing!\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(31908, 'Did you get those claws?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32000, 'Julian\'s revenge'),
(32001, 'Julian in Sand Hill asks you to defeat Prisoners.\n(Search Collapsed Prison and Scaffold Execution Ground)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32002, 'Oh! Hello...\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32003, 'You seem depressed. What\'s gong on? It\'s unlike you.\n[NEXT]'),
(32004, 'Oh... Yes... \nWell, today is the anniversary of my parent\'s death.\n[NEXT]'),
(32005, 'I see, I\'m sorry...\nDo cheer up though... I\'m sure your parents will be happier in heaven if you aren\'t sad. \n[NEXT]'),
(32006, 'Yes, I know... But, when I think of those whom responsible for their death... I cannot help myself but to be furious... Even if they are rotting in prison.\n[NEXT]'),
(32007, 'Prison? You mean one near Elderine...?\n[NEXT]'),
(32008, 'Yes... What? Did something happened to that prison?\n[NEXT]'),
(32009, 'Didn\'t you know? There was a big riot and all the convicts escaped. Oh no, it means those whom responsible for your parent\'s murder escaped also.\n[NEXT]'),
(32010, 'No...!\nIt can\'t be! How can there be a justice, when they are walking free!? NO! \n[BUTTON]=[Julian, stay calm. You must do your duties here. Let me get them for you.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Go get him tiger! Remember eye of tiger!][2]'),
(32011, 'Julian I got them! Every single one of them.\nDon\'t worry about it. They will pay for their sins.\n[NEXT]'),
(32012, 'Thank you. I\'m sure now my parents will rest in peace...\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32013, 'They will pay dearly!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32100, 'Voice of Spirit'),
(32101, 'Paladin Master Keast of Elderine asks you to collect Cursed Spirits from dead tree spirits.\n(Search Collapsed Prision, Damned Souls can be obtained by defeating Dead Tree Souls)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32102, 'Let there will be peace with every step you take. Welcome, [NAME].\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32103, 'Hello Keast.\nHave you summoned me?\n[NEXT]'),
(32104, 'Yes, thank you for coming.\nI have an important task for you.\nDo you think you can carry it out?\n[NEXT]'),
(32105, 'Of course, but I need to know what I am against it first.\n[NEXT]'),
(32106, 'Thank you always.\nThe other night, in my dreams, I witness a vison. In that vision, souls from graves are sucked out of their resting tombs and absorbed into a dead tree souls. In the dead tree, resides many damned and cursed spirits next to a innocent bystanders. Those damned and cursed ones were once good. I need them to be freed. Could you help me with this very important task, [NAME]? Please bring back {color,yellow, Cursed Spirits}.\n[BUTTON]=[Of course. It\'ll be done][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Ghost? NO WAY! crazy or something...][2]'),
(32107, 'Keast! Here\'s the souls I\'ve collected. \n[NEXT]'),
(32108, 'How can such horrible events could occur? These are innocent souls... I need to to pray for 100 days in order to completely free them. Thank you. Because of you [NAME], they are saved. \n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32109, 'Goto {color,yellow,Collapsed Prison} right now!. \n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32200, 'Black Seed'),
(32201, 'Enchanter Master Wishis of Elderine asks you to collect Black Seeds.\n(Search Collapsed Prison. Black Seeds can be obtained by defeating Senior Torturers)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32202, 'How are you\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32203, 'Oh! I was about the go out.\nYes, [NAME] could you help out with something important?\n[NEXT]'),
(32204, 'Important?\nWhat is it?\n[NEXT]'),
(32205, 'Well...\nI\'ve recently acquired very peculiar black seed from a Senior Torturer\'s body. Some of the seeds have already sprouted. I need to find out more about this seed which are feeding off human flesh. \nCould you fetch of these black seeds?\n[BUTTON]=[Sure, not a problem][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I\'m not getting no flesh eating seeds for you.][2]'),
(32206, 'Whisis, I have those seeds for you.\n[NEXT]'),
(32207, 'Thank you. \nI need to study deeper into these seeds. They seem very dangerous for sure. Maybe because of these, he became more evil.\nThank you again for your help [NAME].\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32208, 'It\'s very peculiar to have such seed sprout from a body.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32300, 'Disharken\'s Blue Hides'),
(32301, 'Item Merchant Kenton of Elderine asks you to collect Blue Leathers of Des Harkan.\n(Search Collapsed Prison. Blue Leathers of Disharken can be obtained by defeating Des Harkens.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32302, '[NAME], come over here.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32303, 'What\'s up?\n[NEXT]'),
(32304, 'Remember that I asked you to get some Harken\'s Hides? Well, this time, I want some {color,yellow,Des Harken Skin}. They are even more luxurious and the colors are just deeper. And of course more expensive! \nAnd guess what? You are going to have the honor to contribute to my beautiful masterpiece by getting them for me! \n[BUTTON]=[More expensive? Fine, I\'ll do it but pay me more for it then. ][1] \n[BUTTON]=[Forget you!][2]'),
(32305, 'Hey Kenton, catch!\n[NEXT]'),
(32306, 'Hey honey! Remember to take your prize with you! \n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32307, 'What is it honey?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32400, 'Karasian\'s Magic Scroll'),
(32401, 'Skill Master Cyburn of Uruga asks you to collect Templar\'s Scrolls and Arch Templar\'s Scrolls from (Searched Collapsed Prison. Templar\'s Scrolls and Arch Templar\'s Scrolls can be obtained by defeating Karasian Templars and Karasian Arch Templars) \n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32402, 'Hey, [NAME]. How\'s your journey going?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32403, 'Yes well, same ole\' Always short on something.\n[NEXT]'),
(32404, 'Really? Do you want some part time job so you can earn some extra money?\n[NEXT]'),
(32405, 'Sure! \n[NEXT]'),
(32406, 'Ha Ha Ha Ha! Well, I\'ve been studying into Karasian\'s magics you see. I know he is evil but he did had very ground breaking way of magics. So could I trouble you for {color,yellow, Templar\'s Scrolls, and Arch Templar\'s Scrolls?}\n[BUTTON]=[Roger that!][1]\n[BUTTON]=[No way!][2]'),
(32407, 'Cyburn! I got your scrolls right here! They were really tough...\n[NEXT]'),
(32408, 'For a second I thought you called me a name. Ha Ha Ha, yes they are tough aren\'t they? Karasian\'s magic is pretty strong for sure. \nThank you.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32409, 'Well, did you get it?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32500, 'Why those little!'),
(32501, 'Healer Poring of Uruga asks you to defeat 50 Greenkies and 50 Archons.\n(Search Uruga)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32502, 'How can they do such thing?!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32503, '(Wow, Poring is mad at something)\nHey what\'s going on?\n[NEXT]'),
(32504, 'Oh good timing!\nThose Greenkies and Archons are deliberately eating fairy flowers! At this rate, the fairy flower population will be extincted!\n[NEXT]'),
(32505, 'I didn\'t know they eat them.\n[NEXT]'),
(32506, 'I am furious! I can\'t just sit here and wait. Can you defeat {color,yellow,50 Greenkies} and {color,yellow,50 Archons}? Just destroy them!\n[BUTTON]=[Destroy? Ah, okay I\'ll get\'em.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[What is the wrong with you. They were just eating.][2]'),
(32507, 'Hey like you said, I destroyed them.\n[NEXT]'),
(32508, 'Thank you please to destroy them when you see them in future.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32509, 'I\'ll blow them up!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32600, 'Strength Enhancing Elixir'),
(32601, 'Skill Master Cyburn of Uruga asks you to collect 5 Navar Hairs, 3 Canine Teeth of Giant Sparkdogs, and 2 Lashes of Blue Trumpies.\n(Search Concealed Prison. Navar Hairs, Canine Teeth of Giant Sparkdogs, and Lashes of Blue Clover Trumpies can be obtained by defeating Navars, Giant Sparkdogs, and Blue Clover Trumpies)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32602, 'Good you are here. Take a look at this.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32603, 'It\'s a very pretty pink elixir. Is it a strawberry flavored?\n[NEXT]'),
(32604, 'It looks very girly but, it has real bite to it. I\'ve named it \'Fierce Elixir\'. It\'s recipe was written on that Karasian\'s Scroll you got me not to long ago. \nIt does have bit of draw back though.\n[NEXT]'),
(32605, 'Draw back?\n[NEXT]'),
(32606, 'Ingredients are very difficult to find. I had a hard time gathering ingredient for this prototype. I want to make you one too, if you can get me some necessary ingredients. \nIt\'ll definitely help out in your journey. \nHere\'s the list of needed ingredients:\n{color,yellow,5 Navar Hairs}, {color,yellow,3 Canine Teeth of Giant Sparkdogs}, and {color,yellow,2 Lashes of Blue Clover Trumpies}. Weird ingredients huh?\n[BUTTON]=[Okay, stay put. I\'ll get\'em.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Yes, it\'s weird alright. Too weird.][2]'),
(32607, 'Here it is. It was tough to get them.\n[NEXT]'),
(32608, 'Thanks. You won\'t regret it though. \nOkay then, let\'s see...\nYes, I\'m finished. Take this. When you need them, just drink it with one big gulp. \n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32609, 'I know it\'s hard, but you won\'t regret it.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32700, 'Ancient Powers'),
(32701, 'Town Chief Adrian of Uruga asks you to collect 30 Naiad Demon Heart that contain ancient monster powers.\n(Search Concealed Prison. Naiad Demon Hearts can be obtained by defeating Naiad Demons)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32702, 'Do you know about the great ancient power?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32703, 'ancient power? What are you talking about?\n[NEXT]'),
(32704, 'Yes the ancient power. Once, these land were filled with ancient monsters that are much stronger then the current monsters. In old days, instead of using safety of numbers, there were just small group of very powerful monsters. \n[NEXT]'),
(32705, 'Is there such monsters still around to this date?\n[NEXT]'),
(32706, 'Yes there are.\nThey adapted to new enviorments. They might be smaller stature but they have same lineage to ancient ones. One of the good example is Naiad Demon Monster. It\'s not an easy monster to hunt. That\'s why I\'ve call you. I was wondering if you could get it\'s {color,yellow,Demon Heart}. \n[BUTTON]=[I will.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Are you nuts? No way!][2]'),
(32707, 'Adrian, I got that heart you wanted.\n[NEXT]'),
(32708, 'Thank you. I hope I can find a trace of ancient power with it.\n[NEXT]'),
(32709, 'Heart is where your power is stored. With it many questions can be answered.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32800, 'Don\'t be too Greedy'),
(32801, 'Furniture Shop Owner Forest Tim of Uruga asks you to defeat 80 Greedy Lizardmen and collect 50 Decorative Jewels that he lost. \n(Search Forest of Slumber. Decorative Jewels can be obtained by defeating Greedy Lizardmen)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32802, 'I CAN\'T JUST SIT HERE AND TAKE IT ANYMORE!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32803, '(Whoa, Tim is going nuts)\nWhat\'s going on Tim?\n[NEXT]'),
(32804, 'I can\'t take it anymore. I\'ve been patient from day one! Now, this isn\'t going to do... \nFoods and other shipments, fine I\'ll starve a little, but my furniture decoration shipments?! That\'s just gone too far!\n[NEXT]'),
(32805, 'Hey relax Tim.\nSo I\'m guessing someone took your shipments.\n[NEXT]'),
(32806, 'Yes, those {color,yellow,Greedy Lizardman} hijacked all shipments into the town. I can\'t relax if I wanted to.\n[BUTTON]=[I\'ll get them. You just sit here and breathe][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Maybe you should get into more simple lined furnitures.][2]'),
(32807, 'Tim, I got all those lost decorative jewels.\n[NEXT]'),
(32808, 'Thank you! Now I can\'t finish my pieces.\nI don\'t know what to say.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32809, 'I am furious.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32900, 'Spirit with lost heart'),
(32901, 'Healer Poring of Uruga asks you to defeat 50 Sylphs and collect 10 Sylph\'s Tears.\n(Search Forest of Slumber. Sylph\'s Tears can be obtained by defeating Sylphs)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32902, 'Sobbing...\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(32903, 'What\'s going on Poring? Why are yo crying?\n[NEXT]'),
(32904, 'I have encountered a terrible news.\nHow could this happen?\n[NEXT]'),
(32905, 'What is it? Please tell me...\n[NEXT]'),
(32906, 'Sylph\'s tear should not be created...\nSylph is one of the highest guardian spirit. They were the most pure and lovely spirits.\nBut, they all turned to a monster. It\'s just unthinkable. \nWhen a Sylph nears a death, it creates a jewel called a Sylph\'s tear. If they possess such jewel within their body, it means that they have lost all good within them.\n[NEXT]'),
(32907, 'Don\'t cry. Maybe there are some of the heart left in them.\n[NEXT]'),
(32908, 'Yes, they must. But yesterday, I saw an item merchant who is selling {color,yellow,Sylph\'s Tearss}. It means it has already begun.\nIf it is true, at least we could end their misery. Please [NAME], make them rest in peace. \n[BUTTON]=[I will end their misery, and let them to rest.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Maybe they want to live in whatever form they can.][2]'),
(32909, 'I\'m back. I don\'t have a good news. Look, it\'s Sylph\'s tears.\n[NEXT]'),
(32910, 'I see. Sobs...\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(32911, 'Please, I hope I\'m mistaken.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33000, 'Eye of Sword'),
(33001, 'Skill Master Cyburn of Uruga asks you to collect 1 Dark Eye. \n(Search Concealed Prison. Dark Eyes can be obtained by defeating Cursed Swords)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33002, 'Cyburn!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33003, 'Oh, [NAME], what brings you here?\n[NEXT]'),
(33004, 'I\'ve acqured something odd.\n[NEXT]'),
(33005, 'Hmm...\n[NEXT]'),
(33006, 'What is it?\n[NEXT]'),
(33007, 'All their minds are concentrated and showing in form of an eye. It is a dangerous item. It of course isn\'t part of all {color,yellow,Cursed Swords}, but in any case, any item with their concentrated spirit are dangerous regardless. Even more so, when it is in form of weapon. \n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33008, 'What is it?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33100, 'Magic Arrow'),
(33101, 'Scout Master Deikid of Elderine asks you to collect 60 Magic Arrows to help his research.\n(Search Forest of Slumber. Magic Arrows can be obtained by defeating Diamond Trumpies)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33102, '[NAME]. Do you know which arrow make the best arrow in the world?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33103, 'Mithril! They are light yet strong like a dragon.\n[NEXT]'),
(33104, 'Impressive! You know the basic very well. However there is an arrow that surpasses mithril.\n[NEXT]'),
(33105, 'Really? What is it?\n[NEXT]'),
(33106, 'Magic Arrows. However, regular Magic Arrows are so difficult to control that becomes even useless in battles. \nOne made by {color,yellow,Diamond Trumpies}. Are different then those of regular counterpart. I had a chance to examine one closely, and they were simply superb. I was wondering, if you could collect {color,yellow,60 Magic Arrows}?\n[BUTTON]=[Not a problem.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Maybe next time.][2]'),
(33107, 'Here you go, wow these are really cool arrows.\n[NEXT]'),
(33108, 'Aren\'t they glorious! Thank you for getting these for me. These arrows will help me on my research.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33109, 'Diamond Trumpies can be found at Sleeping Forest\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33200, 'Lost Pieces of Dreams 1'),
(33201, 'Town Chief Roumenus of Roumen asks you to collect 19 Dream Pieces. \n(Search Concealed Prison . Dream Pieces can be obtained by defeating Black Incubuses)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33202, 'When dreams are completely stolen from a child, that child cannot withstand this world.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33203, 'Dreams stolen?\nWhat are you talking about?\n[NEXT]'),
(33204, 'Yes, those terrible afflictions are plaguing Roumen as well. I really thought we will be safe from those damn Black Incubuses. \nYou heard of them right?\n[NEXT]'),
(33205, 'Yes, I have.\nThey are terrible monsters.\n[NEXT]'),
(33206, 'Compare to Uruga or Elderine, Roumen was relatively safe from powerful monster attacks. \nOur children are slowly dying from those terrible demons. \nCould you help us out?\nFor these dying children. Help us wake them from their fatal slumber.\n[NEXT]'),
(33207, 'Fatal slumber? Those children are dying?\nI won\'t forgive those monsters. Praying only on the weak and helpless.\n[NEXT]'),
(33208, 'If the slumber lasts more then 3 days, there aren\'t anything we can do about them. We have 19 children who are afflicted with this conditions since last night. They will slowly die unless we help them. Please, defeat {color,yellow,Black Incubuses} and retrieve {color,yellow,19 Dream Pieces}.\n[BUTTON]=[Don\'t worry I\'ll get them][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I don\'t think I can help out. Sorry.][2]'),
(33209, 'I\'m back. I\'ve found all the dream pieces.\nI didn\'t realize how beautiful today is.\n[NEXT]'),
(33210, 'Oh good you are here! I hope it\'s not too late. \nNow if you leave it out like this, the dreams will return to their rightful owners. Take a look.\nIsn\'t it beautiful?\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33211, 'Please hurry!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33300, 'Lost Pieces of Dreams 2'),
(33301, 'Town Chief Roumenus of Roumen asks you to collect 1 Broken Dream Piece. \n(Search Concealed Prison . Dream Pieces can be obtained by defeating Black Incubuses)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33302, 'How could this happen!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33303, 'What\'s going on? This piece isn\'t returning to its owner.\n[NEXT]'),
(33304, 'This isn\'t a piece of a dream, rather it\'s a Black Incubus\'s trap.\nWe need to find out who this dream belongs to.\n[NEXT]'),
(33305, 'Let me go with you!\n[NEXT]'),
(33306, '<Maria>\nKeira isn\'t waking up. I don\'t know what to do.\n<Roumenous>\nKeira!\n<Maria>\nEveryone recovered, except Keira. What\'s going on Roumenous!?\n[NEXT]'),
(33307, '[NAME], please hurry! Please recover Keira\'s {color,yellow,Broken Dream Piece} from those horrible monster!\n[BUTTON]=[I got this! Don\'t worry!][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I\'ve done all I could. Let it go... What can you do.][2]'),
(33308, 'Roumenous!\nI did retrieve the piece... but...\n[NEXT]'),
(33309, 'What is it! Spit it out!\n[NEXT]'),
(33310, 'I think it\'s broken. It lost it\'s sheen.\n[NEXT]'),
(33311, 'It can\'t be... \nNo! No!\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33312, 'Please let it be safe.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33400, 'Final Rest 1'),
(33401, 'Burning Rock Merchant Master Maxuter received an odd request. You musts defeat Cursed Knights from the Blazing Mines and retrieve \'Luna\'s Breath". (Epic quest)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33402, '[NAME], you are here. Thank you for coming to such a dangerous place.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33403, 'Don\'t worry about it. Is there a request for me?\n[NEXT]'),
(33404, 'Yes, as a matter of fact.\nIt\'s not an easy task. I just don\'t think anyone else but you can take on this quest. Of course difficult tasks equal greater rewards.\n[NEXT]'),
(33405, 'What is it?\n[NEXT]'),
(33406, 'Well, last night a stranger in a cape came to submit a request. That stranger gave me a large sum of money and said the following: {color,yellow,Eliminate the Cursed Knights that reside in the Blazing Mines, and bring back my \'Luna\'s Breath\'}.\nI asked what it was, but stranger did not answer.\nIt\'s really odd.\n[NEXT]'),
(33407, 'Odd? About what?\n[NEXT]'),
(33408, 'The Stranger\'s hands. They were that of a mummified corpse. The stranger disappeared quickly into the night, right after making the request. \nI really don\'t think there is anyone else who is qualified to take on such an odd quest except you. \n{color,yellow,Eliminate the Cursed Knights in the Blazing Mines and bring back \'Luna\'s Breath\'}. \n[BUTTON]=[Don\'t worry, I\'m sure I can find Luna\'s Breath from the Cursed Knights.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[You sure are nuts, taking on total stanger\'s request like that.][2]'),
(33409, 'Maxuter! I got it! Luna\'s Breath.\n[NEXT]'),
(33410, 'You did!?\nWait lemme see!\nThis is!\n(Maxuter gazes into the orb filled with cloudy mist)\nThis is Luna\'s Breath?\n[NEXT]'),
(33411, 'As the Cursed Knight died, it told me to protect the Luna\'s Breath, and dropped this. \n[NEXT]'),
(33412, 'I see.\nI will deliever this as soon as the requester comes back.\nThank you and take this reward.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33413, 'That suspicious traveler told me to \'bring back\' Luna\'s Breath. Not \'find\'. Does that mean it once belonged to that odd traveler?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33500, 'Final Rest 2'),
(33501, 'Maxuter received a mysterious request from an odd traveler. You must defeat Cursed Knight Silvers at the Blazing Mines and retrieve \'Luna\'s Eyes\' (Epic quest).\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33502, '[NAME]!! [NAME]!!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33503, 'Maxuter! Did you find out if what I got for you is in fact \'Luna\'s Breath\'? \n[NEXT]'),
(33504, 'Yes, it was.\nThat stranger made another request. More reward is in it. He now wants you to retrieve {color,yellow,\'Luna\'s Eyes\' from the Cursed Knight Silvers}. \nAgain, he just disappeared right after making the request, so I have very limited information about it.\n[NEXT] '),
(33505, 'I see...\nI will help out, so don\'t worry. They are pretty tough, and not many people can take them on.\n[NEXT]'),
(33506, 'Thank you so much [NAME].\nPlease get {color,yellow,\'Luna\'s Eyes} from the {color,yellow,Cursed Knight Silvers}.\n[BUTTON]=[I\'ll be right back.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Come to think of it, I gotta do something else... ][2]'),
(33507, 'Can this be what that stranger was looking for? The Cursed Knight Silvers were protecting this like it was their own child.\n[NEXT]'),
(33508, 'It seems like it. It should be verified by him though. Thank you.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33509, 'His voice was raspy and sounded like that of a zombie\'s.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33600, 'Final Rest 3'),
(33601, 'Maxuter received an odd request from the strange traveler. You must defeat Cursed Knight Golds and retrieve \'Luna\'s Heart\'\n(Epic quest)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33602, '[NAME], take a look at this!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33603, 'What are all these silvers and potions?\n[NEXT]'),
(33604, 'A reward that stranger left for his new request. \nWhen I handed over the \'Luna\'s Eye\', he stood there, motionless for a long time. Then he said: \'It\'s been a long time since I looked into your eyes...\'. He seemed very sad, like he was about to cry. Then he gave me this and asked to retrieve the \'Luna\'s Heart\' from the Cursed Knight Golds.\n[NEXT]'),
(33605, 'Luna\'s Heart huh?\nWho is this Luna? Why is this Luna so important to him?\n[NEXT]'),
(33606, 'I am also curious about that. One thing for sure, I don\'t think he means any harm. Although he has a horrible voice and appearance, I don\'t believe that he is of evil source. Please, could you get {color,yellow,\'Luna\'s Heart\' from the Cursed Knight Golds}? \n[BUTTON]=[Sure, don\'t worry.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[The Cursed Knight Golds are strong... I don\'t know...][2]'),
(33607, 'Here it is. It definitely is a heart.\n[NEXT]'),
(33608, 'It\'s still alive!\nHow can this be?\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33609, 'I\'m sure he\'s not evil.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33700, 'Final Rest 4'),
(33701, 'Maxuter\'s been receiving odd requests from a mysterious stranger. Let\'s listen to Maxuter\'s story about this person.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33702, '[NAME]... \n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33703, 'Maxuter, were you crying?\nWhat\'s going on?\n[NEXT]'),
(33704, 'Oh well. It\'s nothing.\nNo, it\'s because of this diary.\n[NEXT]'),
(33705, 'Who\'s diary is this?\n[NEXT]'),
(33706, 'It\'s that stranger\'s diary. He gave me this, so I can understand why he\'s desperately seeking those odd objects. I didn\'t believe it at first but, Uruga\'s Adrian told me that the events written in this diary did happened. \nI am in shame that I had a doubt about him. \n[NEXT]'),
(33707, 'Could you tell me what\'s going on?\n[NEXT]'),
(33708, 'I told the stranger about how you have been retrieving all these items, and he asked me to explain what\'s going on to you.\nAbout 100 years ago, when Burning Rock and Flaming Mine were unknown to many, there was a power hungry warlock. This warlock wanted to gain all the world\'s wealth and fame. His evil lust for worldly happiness were backed up by his genius mind. \nHe created a device called the \'Silver Wing\' and traveled the world in search of gold and fame. Then he stumbled upon this land.\n[NEXT]'),
(33709, 'Flaming Mine...\n[NEXT]'),
(33710, 'Yes, all these jewels, ores, and gold from the mine fueled his greed. And then...\n[NEXT]'),
(33711, 'Did he run into guardians?\n[NEXT]'),
(33712, 'He ran into the Cursed Knight Lord, the keeper of all the fortunes in the mines. The Warlock was no match for the Cursed Knight Lord. He was about to meet his imminent death. He overheard a deep desire within Cursed Knight Lord\'s heart.\nThe Cursed Knight Lord wanted death.\n[NEXT]'),
(33713, 'Wanted death? Why?\n[NEXT]'),
(33714, 'Guardians are born to be servants to their task.\nThey live forever, without any rest to fulfill their duties.\nCursed Knights, wanted to end these unending mission. They wanted the rest, that death would bring. \nThis warlock, whom wanted nothing but to survive and be famous, muttered out this nonsense: \'One who possesses a young girl\'s pure soul, rest will come to you\'. \n[NEXT]'),
(33715, 'Unforgivable!\n[NEXT]'),
(33716, 'Yes it is.\nTo the Cursed Knights, the word rest was too attractive to pass up. Without hesitation, the Cursed Knight Lord commanded the dying warlock; \'Bring me one whom possesses such quality, then I\'ll spare you\'. \nThe warlock, who was blinded by fear of death, traveled to town and kidnapped an orphan girl name Luna, who was dubbed as a saint by the town\'s folks. That horrible warlock\'s whereabouts are unknown after that, but the important thing is that an innocent girl lost her soul to the Cursed Knight Lord.\n[NEXT]'),
(33717, 'What happened after that?\n[NEXT]'),
(33718, 'The girl vanished forever. However, there was one person who did not rest to find her. A young man who was betrothed to her since a child, had learned of the story where her soul had been sacrificed to the Cursed Knights.\nA normal person to travel to Burning Rock was an impossible task at the time. He couldn\'t forgive himself for letting his love to be taken away like that. Him being a mear human, and plagued with an 80 year life span, did not help either. You see, he needed more time to reach Burning Rock. \nSo, he had to make the ultimate decision.\n[NEXT]'),
(33719, 'That mummified corpse traveler.\n[NEXT]'),
(33720, 'Yes, it is him. To last more than 200 years, he needed the power from the darkside. He sold his one eye and life to the dark warlock \'Luca\' and received his precious time to search. \nYears passed, and finally the path to Burning Rock had been discovered, and finally he was able to reach me.\n[NEXT]'),
(33721, 'I see. So?\n[NEXT]'),
(33722, 'He doesn\'t have any power except for a walking state of death. He just wants to retrieve Luna\'s soul, so she can finally be freed. That\'s the only thing he desires and hopes. \nThat\'s the only goal for him to exist.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete epic quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33723, '... \n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33800, 'Final Rest 5'),
(33801, 'Maxuter received an odd request from the mysterious traveler. \nYou must defeat the Cursed Knight Lord from the Flaming Mines, and retrieve \'Luna\'s Spirit\'.\n(Epic quest)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33802, 'I know this isn\'t easy and it\'s very dangerous but... \n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33803, 'You want me to take the Cursed Knight Lord out.\n[NEXT]'),
(33804, 'Yes.\nIt\'s an almost impossible task. However, I believe in you, [NAME].\nI know this task can\'t be done by yourself. However, if you team up with other fellow adventurers, you can bring back Luna\'s Spirit. \n[BUTTON]=[I will do whatever I have to do to bring it back.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[It\'s a bit too much for me.][2]'),
(33805, 'Maxuter! The deed is done! We defeated that foul monster.\n[NEXT]'),
(33806, 'I knew you could do it!\nYou have done a wonderful thing!\nYou have done a thing of legend, that\'ll be forever told through generations!!!\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33807, 'I know it is dangerous. Please take this on, not as a request, but as a plea. \n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33900, 'To Swamp of Dawn (Adrian\'s request)'),
(33901, 'Adrian wants to investigate further into the Swamp of Dawn. You must travel to the Swamp of Dawn and investigate monster population. \n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33902, 'Have you heard?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(33903, 'About what?\n[NEXT]'),
(33904, 'About the discovery of the Swamp of Dawn of course!!!\n[NEXT]'),
(33905, 'Oh that...\n(She\'s overly enthusiastic... I never seen her like this before.)\nYes, I have.\n[NEXT]'),
(33906, 'Everyone is raving about it. Of course our town was the first to learn of such wonderful news. We already have a investigator dispatched to the scene as well. \nI was wondering if you could join the investigation. I heard there is a monster called Caiman Junior. I was wondering if you could find more about that monster. I\'m sure if you hunt about 180 of them, you would be able to find more about it. \n[BUTTON]=[Sure thing, right away.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[You are joking right? Ha Ha Ha!][2]'),
(33907, 'Sup Adrian, I found more about that monster.\n[NEXT]'),
(33908, 'Good!\nSo tell me, how was their battle style? Looks? Did they wear any armors or wield any weapons? \nOh, am I asking too fast for you to handle?\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(33909, 'Am I too excited? It\'s very exciting!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34000, 'To Swamp of Dawn (Roumenus\' request)'),
(34001, 'Roumenus wants to investigate further into the Swamp of Dawn. You must travel to the Swamp of Dawn and investigate the monster population. \n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34002, 'Hey! [NAME]! Did you know about it?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34003, 'Let me guess. Swamp of Dawn?\n[NEXT]'),
(34004, 'You do huh? \nThen you know about those Caiman Juniors. right?\n[NEXT]'),
(34005, 'Yes, I have.\n(Why is he overly enthusiastic... I\'ve never seen him like this before.)\n\n[NEXT]'),
(34006, 'Everyone is raving about it. Of course, our town was the first to learn of such wonderful news. We already have an investigator dispatched to the scene as well. \nI was wondering if you could join the investigation?  I heard there is a monster called Caiman Junior.  I was wondering if you could find out more about that monster. I\'m sure if you hunt about 180 of them, you would be able to find more about it. \n[BUTTON]=[Sure thing, right away!][1]\n[BUTTON]=[You are joking right? Ha Ha Ha!][2]'),
(34007, 'Hello Roumenus, I found out more information about that monster.\n[NEXT]'),
(34008, 'Good!\nHow was their battle style? Looks? Did they wear any armors or wield any weapons? \nOh, am I asking too many questions?\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34009, 'It\'s very exciting!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34100, 'To Swamp of Dawn (Elbama\'s request)'),
(34101, 'Elderine\'s lord Elbama has also learned of the existence of \'Swamp of Dawn\'.  You must investigate the monsters in the swamp on his behalf.\n(You must defeat Caiman Jr. and retrieve 10 Thick Croc Skins)\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34102, 'Welcome, [NAME].\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34103, 'Hey! How are you doing?\n(Man, it\'s really hard to have a conversation with him)\n[NEXT]'),
(34104, 'The reason I summoned you is because of the newly discovered \'Swamp of Dawn\'.  I\'m sure you have already ventured out there already.\n[NEXT]'),
(34105, 'Well, Yes I did.\n[NEXT]'),
(34106, 'I too would like you to venture out in behalf of me. What do you say? Could you take on {color,yellow,Caiman Jr.} and retrieve {color,yellow,10 Thick Croc Skins}?\n[BUTTON]=[Ah... Okay.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[What? I just can\'t.][2]'),
(34107, 'My lord, I\'m back. It wasn\'t easy.\n[NEXT]'),
(34108, 'Good. \nThank you for all your troubles. Take this potion too and rest.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34109, 'You know how to get there right?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34200, 'Meeting with Cleo'),
(34201, 'Cleo from the Swamp of Dawn is Maxuter\'s acquaintance. \nShe requests that I deliver her letter to Maxuter, in Burning Rock.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34202, 'Who goes there?!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34203, 'Oh I\'m sorry. I didn\'t mean to startle you.\n[NEXT]'),
(34204, 'Well too late! Anyway, what brings you here? Are you here to investigate as well?\n[NEXT]'),
(34205, 'Well, yes in a way. I mean there were a few requests, but I too am a bit curious about this place.\n[NEXT]'),
(34206, 'I see. I am on an investigation mission as well.  I\'ve been hired by a merchant group. \n[NEXT]'),
(34207, 'Merchant group? Burning Rock\'s Merchant Maxuter\'s group?\n[NEXT]'),
(34208, 'Yes! Wow, what a small world! Do you know Maxuter as well?\n[NEXT]'),
(34209, 'Yes I do.\nI\'ve been through a lot at Burning Rock. \nWe\'ve gotten pretty close through our adventures. \n[NEXT]'),
(34210, 'I see, you must be that adventurer Maxuter always talks about.  \nCould you do me a favor? I have a letter for Maxuter, could you please deliver it for me? \n[BUTTON]=[Sure, not a problem.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[It\'s your chore. Do it yourself.][2]'),
(34211, 'Maxuter! I have mail from Cleo.\n[NEXT]'),
(34212, 'Thank you for delivering this letter! \n[NEXT]'),
(34213, 'No worries.\nI\'ll be on my way then. \nBye.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34214, 'Thank you for helping out.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34300, 'Swamp Hunter Caiman Junior'),
(34301, 'Swamp of Dawn investigator Cleo, needs Caiman Junior teeth. Get 10 Caiman Junior teeth for her.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34302, '[NAME], you are still investigating the Swamp of Dawn huh?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34303, 'Yes, there are still many things I need to know but the Caiman Juniors make it hard to move around.\n[NEXT]'),
(34304, 'I agree. \nOh! I almost forgot, Maxuter had a request for you. Could you gather 10 Caiman Junior teeth and bring them back to me? I\'ll make sure they\'ll get to Maxuter. \n[BUTTON]=[Of course.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I\'ll pass.][2]'),
(34305, 'Cleo, I have those teeth for you.\n[NEXT]'),
(34306, 'Thank you so much. I\'ll make sure they get to Maxuter. Here is your reward.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34307, 'Caiman Juniors are very nasty aren\'t they?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34400, 'Piercing Armor!'),
(34401, 'Marty from Elderine is fascinated with the monsters called Rhinoce recently discovered at the Swamp of Dawn. \nYou must retrieve 1 Rhinoce hide.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34402, 'Hey, [NAME]!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34403, 'Hello, Marty. How have you been?\n[NEXT]'),
(34404, 'You been keeping youself busy ?\n[NEXT]'),
(34405, 'Yes I have. \n[NEXT]'),
(34406, 'Hey, you know about the monster called Rhinoce?  They are single horned beasts with very thick armor-like skin. \nIt would make great armor, can you get me {color,yellow,one of their hides for a prototype}? \n[BUTTON]=[Just one? Sure, why not.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[You talking about that big monster with the big horn on it\'s head? NO WAY!.][2]'),
(34407, 'Marty! I got you that hide you wanted. Man these are tough.\n[NEXT]'),
(34408, 'Nice! Thank you so much! \n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34409, 'What? Don\'t give up on me kid!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34500, 'Rhino\'s Horn'),
(34501, 'Elderine lord Elbama is in need of Rhino\'s horn. \nYou need to deliver 30 Rhino\'s horns\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34502, 'Welcome, [NAME].\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34503, 'Have you summoned me?\n[NEXT]'),
(34504, 'Yes,\nWell, I\'ve needed your service more often these days haven\'t I?\n[NEXT]'),
(34505, 'Well many events have been occurring.\nHow may I be in service this time my lord?\n[NEXT]'),
(34506, 'I am in need of your incredible strength again. \nI have heard that there isn\'t anything stronger then Rhino\'s horn. I believe it\'ll make a perfect lance. \nCould you bring me 30 Rhino\'s horn?\nI will of course, award you well.\n[BUTTON]=[I will.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[No thank you.][2]'),
(34507, 'I\'ve got the horn.\n[NEXT]'),
(34508, 'Thank you.\n(Observes the horn very carefully)\nHere\'s your reward. \n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34509, 'Are you done yet? Could you hurry a little?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34600, 'Caiman\'s Egg'),
(34601, 'Robin from Roumen has been asking for you. Robin is asking you for a Caiman\'s Egg. Let\'s try to get him 5 Caiman\'s Eggs.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34602, 'Hey! What took you so long?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34603, 'What was so urgent!? I ran all the way over here!\n[NEXT]'),
(34604, 'Eggs! I need eggs! \n[NEXT]'),
(34605, 'Well, go get them then.\nYou are senile.\n[NEXT]'),
(34606, 'I DON\'T WANT JUST ANY EGG! I want Caiman\'s eggs! I gotta have them! NOW! \n[BUTTON]=[Crazy old man, alright already, I\'ll get them.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[So you can flatus all over after? No way.][2]'),
(34607, 'Here you go old man.\nYou\'re good now right?!\n[NEXT]'),
(34608, 'What are you talking about [NAME]?\nI didn\'t ask you to get that did I?\nSure, I\'ll take them, what? You only brought five of them?\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34609, 'NOW! NOW! NOW!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34700, 'Completion of Blood Magic'),
(34701, 'According to Wishis from Elderine, some monsters from the Swamp of Dawn have special powers hidden within their blood. \nShe also adds that it is the key to complete \'Blood Magic\'.  You must retreive Caiman\'s blood.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34702, 'Blood magic is a forbidden magic, but that was before the Swamp of Dawn was discovered.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34703, 'Blood magic? \nIt was once forbidden?\n[NEXT]'),
(34704, 'It sure was...\nBlood magic harnesses power from blood of magical beasts. It is a very cruel magic, but because of its power, everyone yearned for it.\nLarge quantities of monster\'s blood and elve\'s blood are needed. \n[NEXT]'),
(34705, 'Elves blood!\n[NEXT]'),
(34706, 'Yes, that is why it is forbidden.\nHowever, monsters from the Swamp of Dawn harness powerful magic within their blood. I believe with their blood alone, I can complete \'Blood Magic\'. \n[NAME], please help me complete this new way to make \'Blood Magic\'. However, please keep it a secret from others. \n[BUTTON]=[I will, don\'t worry.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I can\'t. It is illegal after all.][2]'),
(34707, 'Wishis, I have acquired the blood.\n[NEXT]'),
(34708, 'Were you followed?\nGood. Thank you.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34709, 'Please, be very clandestine.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34800, 'Cruel Hunt'),
(34801, 'Torn bodies of soilders have been found at the swamp.  Deikid of Elderine requests that you must 200 Mudmans who are responsible for such cruel death.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34802, '<Guard>\nHe was found like this...\n<Deikid>\nIt is horrible. I will send 50 archers to the scene right away.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34803, 'Deikid, what\'s going on?  Where are you are sending archers?\n[NEXT]'),
(34804, 'Oh perfect timing! I am about to send a reconnaissance unit to the Swamp of Dawn.\n[NEXT]'),
(34805, 'You are sending in troops to unproven lands?\n[NEXT]'),
(34806, 'Yes. It seems monsters called Mudman are creating havoc down there.\nA week ago, I sent a 20 man unit down to the Swamp of Dawn. Only 7 returned, the rest either perished or are missing.\nIt was the Mudman that did these horrible crimes. It seems they consume Elves. The two who are missing were elves.  However, Mudmans do not eat humans. Human soldiers were found mutilated to death. \nCould you help eliminate these horrible creatures?\n[BUTTON]=[Of course!][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I\'ll pass, I really like living. Ha Ha Ha.][2]'),
(34807, 'Deikid, I\'m back! Did your soldiers return safely as well?\n[NEXT]'),
(34808, 'You are here.\nUnfortunately there were some minor casualties. \nNo matter, the deed has been done and they are punished for their crimes. Thank you for your help.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34809, 'I believe they have ulterior motives behind their flesh consumptions.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34900, 'For Elizabeth'),
(34901, 'Item merchant Kenton wants to ease his dead niece\'s soul with Mudman\'s muds. You must retrieve 3 samples of mud from Mudmans.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34902, 'Poor Elizabeth... \n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(34903, 'Huh?\n(Is Kenton crying?)\nAre you okay?\n[NEXT]'),
(34904, 'Leave me alone. I am too sad.\n[NEXT]'),
(34905, 'Oh really? Okay then, I\'ll leave you.\n(Kenton grabs on, as you leave)\nWhat do you want?\n[NEXT]'),
(34906, 'Today is my beautiful niece Elizabeth\'s anniversary. She was killed around this time of year. She was such a beautiful child, fascinated with beauty care and facial masks. I always wanted give her a special facial mask for her beautiful skins. \nI want to give her a facial mask made of Mudman\'s mud. \n[BUTTON]=[Sure, I will.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[No, I know you\'ll use it.][2]'),
(34907, 'Kenton, here you go. Man that wasn\'t cool at all.\n[NEXT]'),
(34908, 'Thank you, thank you!!! I\'m sure Elizabeth will love this as I\'ll enjoy it! OH hohohohoho!!!\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(34909, 'Oh my gosh! What?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35000, 'Ancient Beings 1'),
(35001, 'New monsters from the Swamp of Dawn are slowly unveiling themselves. One of the these new types of monsters are of ancient spirits who still retain ancient ways and memories. Poring asks for you to retrieve 3 Mandrake leaves.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35002, 'No! It can\'t be! I\'m sure this isn\'t right!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35003, 'Poring! What\'s going on?\n[NEXT]'),
(35004, 'Good, you are here! \nI need your help.\n[NEXT]'),
(35005, 'With what?\n[NEXT]'),
(35006, 'We fairies share a collective mind with ancient spirits; where their pains, tears, joys, and memories reside. \nOne of those ancient spirits is called Mandrake. \nI\'ve received very unsettling news. There is news that the \'monster\' called Mandrake is found at the Swamp of Dawn. \nCould you find more about this monster please.  I really need to know the real identity of Mandrake. Please bring back {color,yellow,3 Mandrake leaves}? \n[BUTTON]=[I will.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I\'ll pass.][2]'),
(35007, 'Poring, I\'ve brought back the leaves. They were one tough monster. \n[NEXT]'),
(35008, 'I see, please take this. Thank you.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35009, 'I don\'t want to believe it.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35100, 'Ancient Beings 2'),
(35101, 'Swamp of Dawn monsters are slowly revealing themselves. \nThere are rumors that even spirit monsters with ancient memories still intact reside there.  Per Poring\'s request, you must defeat 200 Mandrakes, who are the father of ancient spirits.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35102, 'I\'m sure it\'s not him.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35103, 'You are talking about the Mandrakes right?\nI\'m sorry to burst your bubble but they are \'monsters\'.\nIt bared no hesitation to attack, and not a single trace of reasoning can be found among them.\n[NEXT]'),
(35104, 'I see...\nI did know about that as well.\nI knew, once turned, it cannot be reversed.\nI\'ve heard that there were ancient spirits whom took on the powers of darkness. Maybe they feared death.\nPlease, stop them and put an end to their misery. \nMonsters baring the form of the once great Mandrake, is hard to bear.\n[BUTTON]=[I will end their miseries.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I just can\'t. I am sorry.][2]'),
(35105, 'Poring, I ended their suffering\nIt is tragic.\n[NEXT]'),
(35106, 'I am sorry to put you in such a situation.\nHowever, they are no longer what they used to be. \n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35107, 'It is sad, but it can\'t be helped.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35200, 'Evolution or Mutation 1'),
(35201, 'Once just a plant, Mantrap Plants have turned into monsters and hunt men. \nPer Forest Tim\'s request, you must hunt down 200 Mantrap Plants.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35202, 'Mantrap Plants were once normal carnivorous plants.\nThey hunted insects and small rodents.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35203, 'Mantrap Plants? I\'ve never heard of one before.\n[NEXT]'),
(35204, 'It\'s one of the monsters that can be seen at the Swamp of Dawn. That place is filled with new monsters.\n[NEXT]'),
(35205, 'Can you tell me about them?\n[NEXT]'),
(35206, 'They have become very dangerous.\nPlease destroy them.                                                                                                  [BUTTON]=[I will destroy them][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I can\'t forgive them either but, I\'m a bit too weak][2]'),
(35207, 'I\'m back.\nThey were really tough monsters. They had an incredible strength.\n[NEXT]'),
(35208, 'I see.\nThey have mutated fully into monsters.  Hmm... I think more research is needed about them.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35209, 'What do you think happened to them? Do you think they evolved into monsters?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35300, 'Evolution or Mutation 2'),
(35301, 'Mantrap Plants are dangerous and hunt men. \nPer Forest Tim\'s request, you must retrieve 10 Mantrap Plant\'s vines.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35302, 'Welcome.\nI\'ve been expecting you.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35303, 'What is it?\n[NEXT]'),
(35304, 'It\'s about those Mantrap Plants. I need to do further research about them. I need to know if they were turned by the dark force, or is it due to their diet.\n[NEXT]'),
(35305, 'I see...\nIt must be hard for you to take on.\n[NEXT]'),
(35306, 'It can\'t be helped. \nI don\'t want anyone else to lose their life from these plants. \nCould I trouble you for their vines? Could you get me about {color,yellow,10 Mantrap Plant\'s vines}? I need to study further into their strength.\n[BUTTON]=[Not a problem, I\'ll be back!][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I can\'t, I almost got killed by those vines... ][2]'),
(35307, 'Tim, I\'m back.\n[NEXT]'),
(35308, 'Thank you! \nThis is it!\nThey are indeed, very strong. It sure is different from the regular plants.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35309, 'This is torture for me.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35400, 'Evolution or Mutation 3'),
(35401, 'Per Forest Tim\'s request, you must retrieve 50 Mantrap Plant\'s leaves so he can conduct further research on the Mantrap Plants.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35402, 'You came.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35403, 'Is it about another investigation?\n[NEXT]'),
(35404, 'I need to know about their photosynthesis abilities. Could you please get me {color,yellow,50 Mantrap Plant\'s leaves}?\n[BUTTON]=[I will][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Nope!][2]'),
(35405, 'I\'m back. Here are the leaves.\n[NEXT]'),
(35406, 'Thank you. \nNow, let\'s find out about their photosynthesis abilities...\nLets see...\nThis is odd, they are not responding to sunlight. It seems like only way they attain a nutrition is through consuming flesh.\nThey are no longer plants, but a monster.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35407, 'To know it for sure, I need your help.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35500, 'Survival Instinct'),
(35501, 'Poring is about to conclude the results on Mantrap Plant\'s change. \nYou must retrieve Mantrap Plant\'s vines, leaves, and roots.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35502, '[NAME]!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35503, 'Did you summon me?\n[NEXT]'),
(35504, 'Yes,\nForest Tim told me what happened. [NAME], you battled with Mantrap Plants at the Swamp of Dawn.\n[NEXT]'),
(35505, 'Yes. It was a difficult battle but none the less, I had a fruitful outcome.\n[NEXT]'),
(35506, 'I see...\nI had a long conversation with Tim.\nI thought they were just monsters with bodies of spirits. Well, it\'s not all of them. Sprits and Faries are in serious trouble. \n[NAME], could you bring one of each Mantrap Plant\'s vine, leaves, and roots? I really need to find something out.\n[BUTTON]=[Sure thing.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Again? Oh come on! No!][2]'),
(35507, 'I\'ve brought them all.\n[NEXT]'),
(35508, 'You are back!\nPlease bring them to me.\nTake a look at this. First let\'s put leaves, vines and roots together and apply magic.\nLook...\n[NEXT]'),
(35509, 'What? They are slowly coming together!\n[NEXT]'),
(35510, 'Yes, regeneration.\nThese monsters were just regular plants. However, to survive in such dark, harsh environments, they adapted to survive.\nSunlight doesn\'t reach the Swamp of Dawn.  Since photosynthesis was out of the question, they consumed flesh to prolong their lives.\n[NEXT]'),
(35511, 'You are saying that they are not born a monster, but became one to survive.\n[NEXT]'),
(35512, 'Yes.\nIt is sad.\nTo survive, they became savage, their sorrows cannot be cured.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35513, 'Do you think their choice was wise?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35600, 'Raid 1'),
(35601, 'Wereboars raided the merchant group, and took all the silks and armors.\nCleo asks that you hunt down 200 Wereboars, and retrieve 20 tender meats, along with 10 fragrant mushrooms. \n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35602, 'I heard Maxuter\'s merchant group was raided.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35603, 'Oh no! I hope no one got hurt!\n[NEXT]'),
(35604, 'I hope so as well.  We don\'t know the details but, we are in serious trouble. Maxuter\'s merchant was to deliver food supplies, and we completely ran out.\n[NEXT]'),
(35605, 'I\'ll get you some food to survive. Hang on tight, I\'m going to go hunt some Wearboars and bring you back some food.\n[NEXT]'),
(35606, 'Thank you so much. \nI am always in your debt.\n[BUTTON]=[Don\'t worry, I\'ll be back.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Well, then pay up, you deadbeat.][2]'),
(35607, 'Cleo, how do you feel? I\'ve brought something to eat.\n[NEXT]'),
(35608, 'Oh thank you! This should suffice until the merchants get here.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35609, 'I\'m starving. I can eat a whole Wereboar.\nOh! How long have you been standing there?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35700, 'Raid 2'),
(35701, 'Cleo asks you to retrieve armor and silk lost to Wereboars. \nYou must retrieve 30 armors and 10 silks.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35702, 'Were you able to handle the Wereboar?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35703, 'They were indeed strong. If you get caught in their striking distance, you\'ll surely be knocked out.\n[NEXT]'),
(35704, 'I see...\nIf strong warrior like [NAME], had a hard time handling them, I\'m sure merchant group had a no chance against them.\n[NEXT]'),
(35705, 'I think it might take too long to redeliver your supplies.\nWe should try to just retrieve lost goods from them.\n[NEXT]'),
(35706, 'I see...\nCould you help me out please? Can you retrieve those lost armors and silks? Maxuter will reward you for your troubles. \n[BUTTON]=[I got this, don\'t worry.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[You want my service? Pay up first!][2]'),
(35707, 'Cleo, I\'ve got\'em all.\nLuckly they haven\'t touched it yet.\n[NEXT]'),
(35708, 'Oh that\'s great!\nI was really worried about loosing some of the articles. These shipments were headed for Uruga. Maxuter was going to supply us with food, on the way to Uruga with these. Thank you so much for everything.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35709, 'Are you okay with this?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35800, 'Hans Masterpiece'),
(35801, 'Hans from Uruga claims to have made the most beautiful armor of all. \nUnfortunately it went missing along with the Maxuter\'s hijacked cargo. \nLet\'s retrieve the armor from the Wereboars. \n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35802, 'This can\'t be happening! My masterpiece is stolen!!! \n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35803, 'What\'s up?\n[NEXT]'),
(35804, 'They took my armor! My precious armor!\n[NEXT]'),
(35805, 'Hey calm down. Who took your armor?\n[NEXT]'),
(35806, 'Yes, well of course. I\'m calm. THIS IS ME CALM!!!\nThose no good Wereboars HIJACKED MY ARMOR! NOOOOO!!!!\nIt was to be my masterpiece, my final installment of artistic creativity. \nIt was made of gold, emeralds, and moon stones.\nThose Wereboars took my masterpiece. My precious master piece.\n[BUTTON]=[Alright already, I\'ll get them back okay?][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Why didn\'t you guard it well, huh? It\'s your fault.][2]'),
(35807, 'Hey I got it back. It\'s kind of in bad shape, but the important thing is you got it back right?\n[NEXT]'),
(35808, 'It\'s all worn out! All the emeralds are missing too!  It\'s worthless now.\nWhew... Oh well... Thanks for getting it back anyway.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35809, 'I\'ve invested a fortune in that armor!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35900, 'Maxuter\'s Concern'),
(35901, 'Maxuter is worried about Cleo who went to the Swamp of Dawn by herself. \nYou must hunt down 80 of each Mandrake and Mantrap Plants, as well as 50 Wereboars. \n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35902, 'I am so worried about her.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(35903, 'Who are you talking about?\n[NEXT]'),
(35904, '[NAME], you do know Cleo right?\n[NEXT]'),
(35905, 'Of course.  Yes, that place is a bit too dangerous.\n[NEXT]'),
(35906, 'Yes, I think so too.\nHowever, everytime I try to stop her from venturing out there, she insists on going. \nNot too long ago, she was attacked by those Mandrakes, Mantrap Plants, and Wereboars. It\'s too dangerous for her.\n[BUTTON]=[Hmm, maybe I can defeat some of those monsters to ease her research!][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Yes, but what can we do right?][2]'),
(35907, 'Well, I did it.  I\'m sure she\'ll have an easier time now.\n[NEXT]'),
(35908, 'Thank you.\nYour hard work will help her research for sure.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(35909, 'She is so strong headed.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36000, 'Prisoner for sure!'),
(36001, 'An odd young man named Watson is found near Dawn Swamp, let\'s talk to him.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36002, 'What are you doing?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36003, 'Oink, oink... oink, oink...\n[NEXT]'),
(36004, 'Hey! Seriously why do you sound like a pig?  What\'s with your raised arms?\n[NEXT]'),
(36005, '(Young man scans the area very carefully then, screams.)\nWhew! \nShut up and don\'t talk to me! If that Ping Pig finds out, I\'ll be in trouble!\n[NEXT]'),
(36006, 'Huh?\nAre you talking about that pig looking monster over there?\n[NEXT]'),
(36007, 'Sheesh! He\'s coming over here! Just pretend that you don\'t see me! Go away! Just go away!\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36008, 'Oink... \n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36100, 'Curse of the Ping Pig 1'),
(36101, 'It seems Ping Pig has put a curse on the young man, and he cannot lower his arms anymore. To help lift the curse, let\'s steal Ping Pig\'s wand.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36102, 'He\'s gone. Whew!\nHey, you are strong warrior aren\'t ya?\nI bet you can take on some of those darn pigs right?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36103, 'Well, Yes...\nBy the way, what are you doing here?\n[NEXT]'),
(36104, 'I\'m held against my will. They put a curse on me.\n[NEXT]'),
(36105, 'Curse? Those simple monsters can put a curse on people?\n[NEXT]'),
(36106, 'I know right?\nI\'m Watson. I\'m here to research this dreadful place. I was almost done with my research and was about to head home, and then I came across those dreadful creatures.\nThey were too strong for me to take on, and when I was about to run, they used some sort of wand to put a curse on me, a pink wand with hearts. Could you get me those wands? Maybe I can lift this curse with it. \n[BUTTON]=[Sure.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[No, that look suits you.][2]'),
(36107, 'Hey, I got some wands but, I don\'t know which one. They all look different. Which one is it?\n[NEXT]'),
(36108, 'Maybe this one? No? Or this? How the heck do I use this thing?\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36109, 'Come on kid! Help me lift this curse!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36200, 'Curse of the Ping Pig 2'),
(36201, 'Because of the Ping Pig\'s curse, Watson is still stuck with his raised arms.  To lift the curse, you must retrieve a paper with spells. \n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36202, 'Why are your arms still raised? \n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36203, 'Well, can\'t you tell by looking at it?! Apparently a wand by itself cannot lift the curse. Those pigs said something while waving the wand, sounded like a spell. It was something long and complicated, that they would need to read from a note.[NEXT]'),
(36204, 'A note? Then it\'s written down somewhere huh?\n[NEXT]'),
(36205, 'Yes! You are a genius! Please get me that note! Please?!\n[BUTTON]=[Sure! I will get it for you.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Why me? Do it yourself.][2]'),
(36206, 'Hey I got that note, but I can\'t make anything out. It\'s written in a foreign language. Can you read it?\n[NEXT]'),
(36207, 'If you can\'t read it, what makes you think I can? \n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36208, 'Please, please help me!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36300, 'Curse of the Ping Pig 3'),
(36301, 'Because of Ping Pig\'s curse, Watson is still unable to lower his arms. To lift the curse, you must hunt 100 Ping Pigs.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36302, 'This is the last straw!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36303, 'What?\n[NEXT]'),
(36304, 'Kill\'em all! If you kill enough of them, I know they\'ll reveal the cure to this dreadful curse.\n[NEXT]'),
(36305, 'Wait a minute, what if I am cursed like you?\n[NEXT]'),
(36306, 'They don\'t put a curse on you while you are in battle with them. \nThey only cast a curse when they find you eating something. They want the food. It\'s partly my fault eating in front of them.\nPlease, get\'em. I know if you defeat enough of them, you\'ll find a way.\n[BUTTON]=[Okay, stay put.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[No way, what have you done for me lately?][2]'),
(36307, 'Watson, I killed about 100 of them, and they didn\'t say anything. I mean no wand, or spell, nothing...\n[NEXT]'),
(36308, 'What!?  What about me? Don\'t you have a sympathy for fallen comrades?\nIt\'s them! Go away kid. If they find me with you, they\'ll torture me for sure!\nWell, get out of here! Shoosh!\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36309, 'I\'m so tired. My arms hurts and I\'m so hungry.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36400, 'Running into Median'),
(36401, 'You\'ve run into Median in front of a large temple.\nLet\'s talk to her.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36402, 'Oh hi! Nice to meet you!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36403, 'Hi! Nice to meet you too!\n[NEXT]'),
(36404, 'I am Median, a priest in training. \nI\'ve been sent by the Elderine temple to investigate this place. \nWho do you think is responsible for all this?\n[NEXT]'),
(36405, 'I really have no clue.\nI\'m guessing some sort of intelligent life form maybe?\n[NEXT]'),
(36406, 'I feel the same way! I mean who else could it be right? All this craftmanship. I can\'t imagine it would be an accidental creation you know. Something intelligent for sure. \n[NEXT]'),
(36407, 'I guess. Did you see the inside yet?\n[NEXT]'),
(36408, 'No, not yet. I just got here. I\'ve been constantly healing myself, just to get this far. I am beat.\n[NAME], have you been inside yet?\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36409, 'What is it?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36500, 'Median\'s Proposal 1'),
(36501, 'The Temple of Spirit is a mysterious temple layered with many secrets. \nMedian is asking you to investigate the interior of the temple. \nYou must defeat 100 Slugs that reside in the temple.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36502, '[NAME], are you planining to venture inside?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36503, 'Yes, sure.\nIt\'s a bit dark and intimidating but sure.\n[NEXT]'),
(36504, 'In that case, could you investigate what resides inside? Like what type of monsters live in there and such.\n[BUTTON]=[Not a problem, I\'ll be back.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[What are you a chicken? Do it yourself!][2]'),
(36505, 'Median! This is what I found out so far. There are monsters called Slugs near the entrance, and they look like this...\n[NEXT]'),
(36506, 'I see... I\'ve never seen anything like this before.\nI know Swamp of Dawn is filled with new monsters.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36507, 'What did it look like inside? Was it cool?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36600, 'Median\'s Proposal 2'),
(36601, 'The Temple of Spirit is a mysterious temple layered with many secrets. \nMedian is asking you to investigate the interior of the temple. \nYou must defeat 150 more Slugs within the temple.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36602, 'Since you have started to investigate the temple, could you do me a favor?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36603, 'Huh? What?\n[NEXT]'),
(36604, 'To tell you the truth, I don\'t have any battle experience. My expertise is in healing power. So, I can only rely on your investigations.\n[NEXT]'),
(36605, 'Oh, don\'t worry about it. I can help you out. Is there anything else you want to know abou this place?\n[NEXT]'),
(36606, 'I know you\'ve encountered those slugs already. Well, I need more data on their battle abilities. Could you defeat about 150 of those Slugs and find more about them?\n[BUTTON]=[Sure, hang on.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[150? Are you nuts?][2]'),
(36607, 'Yo Median! I\'m back!\nIt wasn\'t that bad of a battle. I thought it was relatively easy.\n[NEXT]'),
(36608, 'Thank goodness you are back. It\'s good to hear that they are relatively easy to take on. Of course, I know I can\'t take them on.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36609, 'Did you find more about Slugs?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36700, 'Median\'s Proposal 3'),
(36701, 'To know more about the Slugs, Median is asking for Slug Shells and also their discharge.  Please gather 10 Slug Shells and 10 Slug\'s Juice\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36702, 'So, they look something like this?\n(Draws a Slug on the floor)\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36703, 'Well, let me copy this drawing over to a scroll.\nOh! I also need to find out about the composition of these Slugs. For that, I would need shells and some sort of slime or mucus from it.  Could you get 10 of each? I will reward you well of course. \nI\'ll also inform the Elderine guards so that you\'ll claim an extra reward. \n[BUTTON]=[Oh thanks, I\'ll help you out of course.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I\'m rich enough and busy enough. \'Nuff said.][2]'),
(36704, 'Median! I got those shells and juice you wanted. \nMan it is slimy and nasty. Be careful handling them, it seems like it has acidic properties.\n[NEXT]'),
(36705, 'Oh, they are dangerous things. I should put them in reinforced containers.\nThank you so much.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36706, 'Did you get it?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36800, 'Receiving Extra Rewards'),
(36801, 'Here is a chance to obtain an extra reward from Elderine guards, promised by Median.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36802, 'Are you the one called, [NAME]?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36803, 'Yes, Median told me to travel this way...\n[NEXT]'),
(36804, '(Scanning from head to toe)\nI can\'t believe a person like you actually waltzed into Temple of Spirit. Oh, well, an order is an order. \n[NEXT]'),
(36805, 'Okay...\n[NEXT]'),
(36806, 'Here, take it. \nI\'m sure you\'ve never seen such a thing before. Let me show you what it is. It\'s a high level HP potion.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36807, 'What is it?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36900, 'Median\'s Proposal 4'),
(36901, 'To study Slugs even further , Median is asking for their Antennas and Spines.\nYou must retrieve 10 of each Antennas and 10 Spines.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36902, '[NAME]!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(36903, 'How\'s your research going?\n[NEXT]'),
(36904, 'Well, it\'s kind of at a halt. \nWhen you weren\'t around, I kind of snuck into the entrance of the temple, but I got hit by one of the Slug\'s antennas and got knocked out. I managed to run away.\n[NEXT]'),
(36905, 'That was a close call.\n[NEXT]'),
(36906, 'So, I was wondering if you could get some of their Antennas and Spines? I was in charge of preliminary investigation and I actually need more data. \nI\'m planning to take those Antennas and spines back to Elderine. \n[BUTTON]=[Sure thing. Stay put.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Sorry, but I can\'t help you out.][2]'),
(36907, 'Hey Median, I got them for you.\n[NEXT]'),
(36908, 'Thank you so much. I need to return to Elderine now. Oh and don\'t forget to receive an extra reward from that Elderine guard okay?\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(36909, 'What\'s going on? Is there something wrong?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37000, 'The Terrible Rhinoce Lord'),
(37001, 'Cyburn from Uruga is asking you to eliminate 160 Rhinoce Lords plaguing the Swamp of Dawn.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37002, 'So, have you found out enough to grasp the scope of the Swamp of Dawn?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37003, 'Well, Yes. Not all, but yes just about.\n[NEXT]'),
(37004, 'I\'m guessing you have run into the Rhinoce Lord by now right?\n[NEXT]'),
(37005, 'Well, Yes. I think so. I haven\'t fully encountered all of them yet.\n[NEXT]'),
(37006, 'The Rhinoce Lord is also dubbed as a tyrant of the Rhinoce lineage. \nThey are smart, determined, and strong. Also, they are so short tempered that they\'ll attack even their own kind. \nWhat do you think? Do you think you can handle a couple of these Rhinoce Lords? I know there are tons of them out there but, killing about 160 of them would keep them in check. \n[BUTTON]=[Not a problem, leave it to me!][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I don\'t know about that.][2]'),
(37007, 'Oh man, they were really tough.\n[NEXT]'),
(37008, 'So, how was the battle? Were they strong enough? Thanks for all your troubles.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37009, 'Hey, did you kill all 160 yet?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37100, 'Great Helmet'),
(37101, 'Elderine Guard Nus wants to get a Rhinoce Lord\'s helmet for himself. Why don\'t we do this young fool a favor and get it for him.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37102, 'You been to it huh?! Yes you did!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37103, 'What are you talking about Nus?\n[NEXT]'),
(37104, 'Swamp of Dawn! You been to it.\n[NEXT]'),
(37105, 'Ah! Yes of course. \nWhat about it?\n[NEXT]'),
(37106, 'That means that you fought Rhinoce Lords too huh? \nYou seen their armor in action then huh? How was it? Was it cool? I never seen any other armor that is so cool! I know their armor will be too big for me, but could you at least get me that helmet? \nI really, really want one.\n[BUTTON]=[Okay, I\'ll get one Nus, but get ready to pay up.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Get lost!][2]'),
(37107, 'Here Nus, It wasn\'t easy to get one of these. So, don\'t you go lose it.\n[NEXT]'),
(37108, 'So cool! Wow do I look awesome or what?\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37109, 'Huh?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37200, 'Deformed Monster'),
(37201, 'Roumen\'s Skill Master Ruby is visiting Temple of Spirit with the Roumen town expedition. \nRuby is asking for 30 Mad Slug\'s eggs.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37202, 'Welcome, [NAME].\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37203, 'Hello, Ruby. It\'s been a while.\n[NEXT]'),
(37204, 'It sure has been.\nI know you\'ve become a strong warrior, but don\'t forget your old friends from your novice days.\n[NEXT]'),
(37205, 'Oh, sure. Ha Ha Ha! \n(Wow, Ruby has become quite talkative)\n[NEXT]'),
(37206, 'Anyways, I have been to the Temple of Spirit lately. Have you visited that place yet?\n[NEXT]'),
(37207, 'Yes I have. It was filled with various odd monsters.\n[NEXT]'),
(37208, 'It sure was. There, I found a couple of odd, deformed monsters as well. \nHave you seen Mad Slugs? The slug with the body of a star fish.\n[NEXT]'),
(37209, 'Mad slugs, Yes I did.\nI haven\'t really dealt with them before though. It was bit on the gross side.\n[NEXT]'),
(37210, 'Yes it is.\nOne thing that bothers me is that it had a body of a sea creature instead of snail related creatures. \nIt almost feels as if it was fused with two different species. I\'m sure it means that these monsters are of the ancient creatures.  I need to find more about them. \nI was wondering if you could retrieve about 30 of the Mad Slug\'s eggs. \n[BUTTON]=[Sure thing.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[It\'s called MAD slugs! No way!][2]'),
(37211, 'Here you go. Be careful with it, it\'s a bit slimy.\n[NEXT]'),
(37212, 'It is quite slimy...\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37213, 'Did you find those eggs?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37300, 'Dark Shadow that protects the Temple'),
(37301, 'Elderine\'s lord Elbama lost all of his 20 expeditions members and 10 mercenaries he sent to Temple of Soul. \nPer Elbama\'s request, you must defeat the monster called Shadow that protects the temple and bring back 50 of their symbols.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37302, 'Welcome, you always look so cheerful.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37303, 'Thank you my lord. I always try to stay positive. What does my lord desire from me?\n[NEXT]'),
(37304, 'You don\'t have to be so formal with me. \nIt\'s about Temple of Soul at Dawn Swamp. I\'ve heard you are a quite an expert of that region.\n[NEXT]'),
(37305, 'Well, I don\'t know about being an expert, but I\'ve been to it couple of times.\n[NEXT]'),
(37306, 'Don\'t be mad. It\'s not that big of a deal. \nLately I\'ve been under a lot of stress. It\'s causing me to break out. I want to make a special Aloe Cleanser to help my skin. The problem is that {color,yellow,Aloes} are located in {color,yellow,Collapsed Prison} where the creature {color,yellow,Des Harken} lurks. \nYou may lack fashion sense, but you are one strong fighter! [NAME], could you collect {color,yellow,10 Aloes} for me? \n[BUTTON]=[I\'ll help you out.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I\'m going to buy a new outfit.][2]'),
(37307, 'I\'m back. I\'ve brought back those symbols you wanted too.\n[NEXT]'),
(37308, 'Let\'s see...\nThank you. That monster killed my expedition, so I was bit worried that you will meet the same fate. I\'m glad that you\'ve survived.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37309, 'Did you bring it? Until, you are finished with that job, do not bother me.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37400, 'Man-Eating plant Laplan'),
(37401, 'Cleo is asking you to defeat the man-eating plant called Laplan. You must defeat Laplan and retrieve 60 of it\'s petals.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37402, 'Have you seen a creature called Laplan?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37403, 'Laplan? Yes, that plant with a weird self indulgent fever right?\n[NEXT]'),
(37404, 'Yes, you are right.\nThey are very dangerous monsters. I\'m sure they are the strongest plant around Swamp of Dawn.\n[NEXT]'),
(37405, 'Really? I\'ve never really fought with it before.\n[NEXT]'),
(37406, 'I\'m sure you\'ll take them on from now on. Their petals can earn you great rewards. \nI\'m requesting you bring me 60 of their petals. I\'ll pay of course. \n[BUTTON]=[Sure thing, as long as it pays well!][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I don\'t feel like working right now.][2]'),
(37407, 'Here\'s Laplan\'s petals. They are huge and beautiful.\n[NEXT]'),
(37408, 'Aren\'t they?\nTo tell you the truth, it was a special request from a very important lady. I really don\'t know why they want this, but it does pay the bills.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37409, 'Did you get those petals?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37500, 'How Dare You Copy Me!'),
(37501, 'Poring\'s \'Fairy Flowers\' look a lot like Laplan\'s petals. \nPoring wants you to destroy 200 Laplans.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37502, 'Hmph! I can\'t believe this!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37503, 'Poring? What\'s going on?\n[NEXT]'),
(37504, 'Good timing! You heard of Laplans right?\n[NEXT]'),
(37505, 'Yes, of course. That monster who\'s full of itself.\n[NEXT]'),
(37506, 'EXACTLY!\nI heard those no good monsters abuse flowers! Now they have mimicked the look of my favorite Fairy Flowers. How dare they!\nI want to destroy them!\n[BUTTON]=[You want me to destroy them for you right?][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Yes go get\'em yourself! Go on girl!][2]'),
(37507, 'I did it. It wasn\'t easy.\n[NEXT]'),
(37508, 'Thank you so much! You don\'t know what this means to me.  It was one of the most horrible creatures I have ever encountered. I mean what kind of monster swallows anything whole and alive?\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37509, 'Those no good monsters! I will grind them to bits.\nOh! When did you get here?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37600, 'Purgatory and their cries 1'),
(37601, 'Adrian, chief of Uruga, learns of the suffering cries of souls in purgatory near the Temple of Spirit. \nYou must defeat 200 Red Shadows at the Temple of Spirit.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37602, 'How does it feel to do something that isn\'t true to your heart?\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37603, 'What do you mean?\n[NEXT]'),
(37604, 'I\'m just curious.\nI wonder how it feels to do things that you do not wish to be part of.\nWhat if your body does the things your mind does not want to partake in?\n[NEXT]'),
(37605, 'It would be horrible. \n[NEXT]'),
(37606, 'It would be indeed, horrible.\nIt wouldn\'t be living, but a torture. \nThe years they spend doing the things they\'ve done, would be a torture for them.\n[NEXT]'),
(37607, 'What are you talking about chief?\n[NEXT]'),
(37608, 'At the Temple of Spirit, there are monsters called Red Shadows. In reality, they aren\'t really monsters, but rather high spirits whom turned to what they are now.\n[NEXT]'),
(37609, 'Spirits turned to monsters? How could it be? \nWait a minute. I did hear about a plant who evolved itself to a monster in order to survive.\n[NEXT]'),
(37610, 'You are right, there are beings who turn into monsters to survive.  But, these shadows have a little bit of a different history behind them. \nShadows were forced into their present state.  They used to be holy guardians of the temple.\n[NEXT]'),
(37611, 'How did they?\n[NEXT]'),
(37612, 'I was able to witness what happened at the temple. All those years they spent trapped as a monster, caused them suffering. They were ancient guardians of the temple, and now the temple lost its purpose, they are trying to fulfill their desires by murderous acts.  We can ease their suffering with their demise.\n[NAME], please end their sufferings and bring them a final rest.\n[BUTTON]=[I will guide them to their rest.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Maybe they prefer life, even in form of a monster.][2]'),
(37613, 'I did it chief. The deed is done.\n[NEXT]'),
(37614, 'Oh you are back.\nI was worried that, it would be too much for you.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37615, 'Ah!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37700, 'Purgatory and their cries 2'),
(37701, 'Adrian, chief of Uruga, learns of the suffering cries of souls in purgatory near the Temple of Spirit. \nYou must defeat Red Shadows at the Temple of Spirit and bring back a Restrained Heart.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37702, '[NAME]!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37703, 'Yes, what is it?\n[NEXT]'),
(37704, 'I figured it out.\n[NEXT]'),
(37705, 'What?\n[NEXT]'),
(37706, 'I\'ve found clues from what they have left behind. Please keep this between you and I, and don\'t tell anyone.\n[NEXT]'),
(37707, 'Your secret is safe with me.\n[NEXT]'),
(37708, 'In old days, there were ancient elves at these temples.\n[NEXT]'),
(37709, 'Are these elves different from of those from Elderine?\n[NEXT]'),
(37710, 'Not many know about these tales from the old days. \nYou are right [NAME], they are ancient beings who are different from those that originated from Elderine. \nHumans came to this continent when Elderine was born and when a great war had already begun.\n[NEXT]'),
(37711, 'That means this Temple of Soul proceeds Elderine\'s time and even goes way back to the time of ancient elf Elga\'s era.\n[NEXT]'),
(37712, 'That\'s right. Lord Elbama desperately wants to find out about the origin of the Temple of Spirit. However, unless he sees through the clues they left behind, he\'ll never figure it out. I\'m sure he already sent a priest to investigate.\n[NEXT]'),
(37713, '(He\'s talking about Median)\nYes, you are right.\n[NEXT]'),
(37714, 'I\'m sure the priest he sent did not have a clue where to look. Only things the priest probably investigated would\'ve been structual analysis or monster populations. I have lived a long time as an Elf, and my time in this world allowed me to witness a glimpse of their pain and sorrows to find such clues to the past of this place.\n[NEXT]'),
(37715, 'I see...\n[NEXT]'),
(37716, 'I\'m sure they\'ll find out in the future, but I\'ll start the process. \n[NAME], I need to know more about their confinement spells. Their state of purgatory is due to an ancient Elves\' spell.  If this dangerous spell falls into the wrong hands, there is no telling what sort of damages it might cause.  I myself, do not want to believe this, but Elves do fall into temptation in front of such power. Such events should never occur. \nPlease, investigate Red Shadows and find the origin of their spells, and bring it back to me.\n[BUTTON]=[I will help you.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I can\'t... What if you fall into temptations too?][2]'),
(37717, 'I\'ve found a heart.  It\'s still beating and covered with foreign text.\n[NEXT]'),
(37718, 'Ah...\nThis is the heart that is restrained.\nThrough this one heart, hundreds of Red Shadows now walk in purgatory. I will study this heart and find a way to undo its binds. \nI might ask your services again in the future. Please help to free those who are suffering. For the peace and glory for this world.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37719, 'We need to find the way to unbind them.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37800, 'Secrets of Tear\'s Marsh 1'),
(37801, 'Adrian and her team of investigators are hard at work to Tear\'s Marsh.\nYou must defeat 10 of each: Dungeon Cayman Junior, Dungeon Rhinos, and Dungeon Cayman at Tear\'s Marsh.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37802, '[NAME]!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37803, 'You have summoned me?\n[NEXT]'),
(37804, 'Thank you for coming on such short notice. I\'m not sure if you already know this but, do you know about Tear\'s Marsh?\n[NEXT]'),
(37805, 'Yes, another swamp-like place further down from the Swamp of Dawn right?\n[NEXT]'),
(37806, 'Right...\nMonsters from that place are stronger then those from the Swamp of Dawn.  \nI wanted to further investigate that place, but all the patrols I\'ve sent escaped barely with their lives intact. \n[NAME], could you help me investigate this place?\nI need you to battle and defeat 20 of each {color,yellow,Dungeon Cayman Junior, Dungeon Rhinos,and Dungeon Cayman}.\n[BUTTON]=[Sure thing, leave it to me.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I don\'t think I can handle that just yet.][2]'),
(37807, 'I\'m back. \nThey were definitely different from those monsters of the Swamp of Dawn. Although they did look similar.\n[NEXT]'),
(37808, 'I see... What else did you find out? Did they use any odd items or talk in different dialect?\nI\'m sorry to flood you with so many questions at once.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37809, 'Is your investigation ready?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37900, 'Secrets of Tear\'s Marsh 2'),
(37901, 'Adrian and her team of investigators are hard at work to study Tear\'s Marsh.\nAdrian learns the past of Tear\'s Marsh. You must defeat Dungeon Rhinoce Lords and Dungeon Laplans to retrieve the Sign of Offering.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37902, 'I was able to find a couple of things.\n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(37903, 'What did you find out?\n[NEXT]'),
(37904, 'I\'m not entirely sure yet, but it seems Tear\'s Marsh, Swamp of Dawn and the Temple of Spirit were once by the seashore. \n[NEXT]'),
(37905, 'These places were by the sea? And?\n[NEXT]'),
(37906, 'And, it looks as if very cruel {color,yellow,sacrificial ceremonys} were held at these places.\n[NEXT]'),
(37907, 'Sacrificial ceremony? I never thought...\n[NEXT]'),
(37908, 'Yes...\nVery cruel practices carried out by the former inhabitants of these places. Nothing is of certain now, but the only thing we can know for certain is that they were capable of doing such brutal acts. \nOne of my men is on his way to bringing back an artifact. I\'m sure after he arrives, more answers can be found out. However, we need more artifacts to draw a more complete conclusion.\n[NEXT]'),
(37909, 'I\'m sure monsters from that region will carry such artifacts with them.\n[NEXT]'),
(37910, 'You are right. \nCould you travel to Tear\'s Marsh and bring back {color,yellow,ancient artififacts that Dungeon Rhinoce Lord and Dungeon Laplan carry}? It doesn\'t matter what kind of artifacts, just anything.\n[BUTTON]=[Okay I will.][1]\n[BUTTON]=[I don\'t think so.][2]'),
(37911, 'Look Adrian, I got this from those monsters. Looks like a Sign of Offering. It seems they offered a live sacrifice to these monsters.\n[NEXT]'),
(37912, 'Yes it seems that way...\nWho were these people? Why would they offer their kind to these monsters? Whose tear is it that flows through Tear\'s Marsh?\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(37913, 'Yes?\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(38000, 'Secrets of Tear\'s Marsh 3'),
(38001, 'Adrian has stumbled upon the secrets of the ancients, and she went to face it by herself. Unfortunately she ran across a Dungeon Caiman Giant and had to flee in a hurry. \nYou must defeat a Dungeon Caiman Giant and bring Adrian\'s staff back.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(38002, 'Hugh, sighs... \n[BUTTON]=[Begin the Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(38003, 'Adrian! What happened?\n[NEXT]'),
(38004, 'Who? What?\n[NEXT]'),
(38005, 'It\'s me, [NAME]! What happened?\n[NEXT]'),
(38006, 'I\'m... I... I\'m okay. I need water... \n[NEXT]'),
(38007, 'Here drink it. What happened? Who did this to you?\n[NEXT]'),
(38008, 'Thank you [NAME].\nI was foolish enough to venture out to Tear\'s Marsh alone. I can\'t tell you why I was there just yet. It is about what happened there before. And I ran into this dangerous monster. Huh?! My staff is gone!\n[NEXT]'),
(38009, 'Your staff? The one you always carry?\n[NEXT]'),
(38010, 'Oh no... \nI was defending myself when that monster try to swallow me whole. It must have swallowed my staff.\nIt\'s a very precious staff that has been handed down through generations. It has special power within that staff. I need that staff back. [NAME], {color,yellow,could you retrieve my staff from a Dungeon Caiman Giant}?\n[BUTTON]=[Of course, why don\'t you go rest while I get it..][1]\n[BUTTON]=[You lost it, you find it.][2]'),
(38011, 'Here\'s your staff back. Luckily it\'s still in one piece.\n[NEXT]'),
(38012, 'Thank you.\nI\'m sorry to keep handing out such harsh tasks to you like that.\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete the Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(38013, 'I need that staff to help protect Uruga! Please get it back.\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(38100, 'Kid Woz\'s Christmas (Event Quest)'),
(38101, 'Cute little Kid Woz from Elderine. \nHe wants to give chocolate to his girlfriend this Christmas. \nGet the Christmas Stocking Chocolate for Woz. \n(Search the Free Battle Zone.) \n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(38102, 'Dashing through the snow,  in a one horse open sleigh~\nOh?! [NAME]!!\n[BUTTON]=[Begin Quest][1]\n[MENU]'),
(38103, 'Ahahaha.  Woz, you are singing a Christmas carol.\nI know that song too.\nThe next line is...\nO\'er the hills we go, laughing all the way (Ha Ha Ha).\nIt is one of the best Christmas carols for Christmas.\nDoesn\'t it get you into the Christmas Spirit?\n[NEXT]'),
(38104, 'You think so too? \nOh, by the way, I wrote a letter to Santa for a Christmas present. \n[NEXT]'),
(38105, 'Oh really? Let me see... \nChristmas Stocking Chocolate? \nWhat\'s that? \n[NEXT]'),
(38106, 'What is what?  It is just chocolate shaped like a stocking.  The truth is, it is for a girl, who I am very interested in... I heard she likes chocolate, so I want to give it to her as a Christmas present.\nThat\'s why I told Santa I want to have chocolate as my Christmas gift.\n[BUTTON]=[(lump in my throat) Cute little boy, let me get that for you. 30 should be enough, right?][1]\n[BUTTON]=[Santa will grant your wish.][2]'),
(38107, 'Woz! Is this the chocolate that you were talking about?\nI got the Chocolate Stocking so I think it\'s okay to ask for another present from Santa.\n[NEXT]'),
(38108, 'Oh, great!! [NAME] You are the best!! Cool! Thanks!\nI will give you a reward for this.  Here is a Santa Hat.  Isn\'t it nice?\nPey made this last year.  I want to give it to you, [NAME].\n\n[BUTTON]=[Complete Quest][1]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
(38109, 'Hey? Did you send my letter to Santa?\nI hope Christmas comes fast.\nJingle bells, Jingle bells, Jingle all the way!\n[BUTTON]=[Continue][1]\n[MENU]'),
(38200, '?????? ?????? ????????(?????? ??????)'),
(38201, '???????? ???????? ???????? ?????? ???? ?????????? ???? ???????? ????, ?????? ???? ?????? ?????? ?????? ???? ???? ??????????.\n???? ???????? ???? ???????? ???? ?????? ?????? ??????.\n[LINE]\n[SHOW_REWARD]'),
